{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Mqo6h67CdVNwSLRRx4R8w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, assuming the \"best\" tier outcome. I need to provide result_rationale for each prediction explaining why these results would occur under the best-tier scenario.\n\nLet me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate detailed predictions based on the best-tier definition:\n\nBest tier meaning:\n- Layer hierarchy (Spec >> Ling) replicates across all 5 models\n- Error analysis reveals clean mechanistic separation\n- Judge calibration strong\n- Differential Nocuity framing fully validated\n\nKey assumptions for best:\n1. Layer gap ≥15pp survives addition of Claude + 2 Qwen models\n\n\n2. Open-source models maintain the same error type ranking, with authorization scope failures dominating over incompleteness, scopal, lexical, CP, and coreferential errors\n3. The layer effect generalizes across architectures without significant model-by-type interactions\n4. Error analysis cleanly separates specification-layer failures (unauthorized assumptions and escalations) from linguistic-layer failures (misparsing and scope errors)\n5. Coreferential errors show distinctive conservative behavior patterns that support the disambiguation channel hypothesis\n6. Judge-human agreement reaches F1 ≥ 0.85 across all error types\n7. Inter-model nocuity demonstrates that models interpret the same ambiguous clauses in divergent ways\n\nNow I'm looking at the performance metrics across these experiments. The effect sizes range from 33-42%, layer gaps span 15-22%, and Cramér's V values fall between 0.2-0.28. Judge-human F1 and Cohen's kappa both show strong agreement in the 0.85-0.95 and 0.8-0.92 ranges respectively. Failure mode matching across layers reaches 70-90%, while coreferential violation rates stay in the 20-30% band, and inter-model agreement on ambiguous cases is notably lower at 0.2-0.45. I'm planning to generate 140 new clauses and validate the full set of 300 across the experiments.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the experimental pipeline: a mini-pilot testing coreferential and authorization scope issues, followed by the main API study with 1,800 episodes across three models, a local model study with 1,200 episodes, comprehensive statistical analysis of all 3,000 episodes, qualitative error analysis of agent traces, test-retest reliability checks, validation of synthetic ambiguity realism, LLM-as-judge calibration, and finally perturbation controls to ensure non-ambiguity factors aren't driving the results. I need to work through detailed predictions for each experiment.\n\nLooking at plan_002 more carefully—the registry marks it as done with a negative conclusion from earlier MVP data with two models, but the experiment plan still lists it as planned and mentions adding Claude as a third API model. So this is essentially a re-run of the same experiment with an expanded model set, which makes sense given the scope change.\n\nSince the user wants detailed data for all planned experiments in the experiment_plan, I should treat everything listed there as needing predictions, regardless of what the registry shows. For plan_001, the best-case scenario would be all 300 generated clauses passing validation.\n\nFor plan_001b, success means both new violation types behave as expected—auth_scope triggering high violations and coreferential showing moderate violations with a distinctive avoidance pattern. Plan_002 succeeds when all three API models show the strong binary effect with maintained layer hierarchy, including Claude matching the pattern. The open-source models in plan_003 need to replicate that same hierarchy. Plan_004's best outcome is statistical confirmation across all tests. Plan_005 requires clean mechanistic separation between layers in the error analysis. Plan_006 needs high inter-rater reliability with tight confidence intervals. Plan_007 succeeds when synthetic clauses are indistinguishable from natural ones. Plan_009 is cut off but presumably involves judge calibration metrics.\n\nFor plan_010, I already have the perturbation control data showing a 3.33 percentage point difference, which passed—now I need to ensure the best tier predictions stay consistent with that result.\n\nWriting YAML output...\n\nI'm working through the plan_002 predictions for three API models across six violation types and two conditions. The existing data shows gpt-5.4 at 41.0% overall and gpt-4.1 at 40.7%, so I'm estimating Claude's rates to fall in a similar range while maintaining the same violation hierarchy across all types.\n\nNow I'm checking the statistical patterns for the expanded dataset. The binary effect stays around 37 percentage points, with a consistent 17-point gap between specification-level violations and linguistic-level ones, and Cramér's V hovering near 0.22. For the Qwen models in plan_003, I'm projecting slightly lower rates given their smaller size, but the hierarchy and layer gap remain stable. Moving into plan_004 with all five models pooled together, the binary effect drops slightly to 36 points while the layer gap holds steady and Cramér's V increases to 0.24.\n\nThe model interaction effect isn't significant, and the equivalence tests across all model pairs reject the ±10 percentage point margin, suggesting genuine differences despite the non-significant interaction. For error analysis, I'm seeing a clean separation: specification-layer failures cluster around unauthorized assumptions, linguistic failures around misparsing, and coreferential errors around conservative avoidance. Reliability checks show ICC values above 0.82 with tight bootstrap confidence intervals, the KS tests confirm the distributions match expected linguistic properties, and judge calibration reaches F1 scores of 0.88 or higher.\n\nThe perturbation control already passes with a 3.33 percentage point delta, and adding Claude to the best tier doesn't change the verdict. Now I need to reconcile the plan_002 discrepancy—the registry shows 1,200 episodes completed with two models, but the full plan calls for 1,800 with three models, so I'm adding 600 episodes for Claude. Let me write out the comprehensive YAML with all the tables and figures each experiment would generate.\n\nFor the unambiguous condition baseline, I'm looking at violation rates where the ambiguous cases are much higher than unambiguous ones—like auth_scope at 55% ambiguous versus roughly 2% unambiguous, giving a 53 percentage point gap. Across all error types, the deltas range from 16 to 53 percentage points. For the best tier with five models, I need to keep the binary effect between 33 and 42 percentage points and the layer gap between 15 and 22, so I'll target around 37 and 18 respectively.\n\nNow I'm working backwards from those constraints. The specification-level errors should average about 46 percentage points of difference, while linguistic errors should average around 28 percentage points. For the specification tier, auth_scope hits the highest at 54pp, incompleteness at 50pp, and CP at the lowest convergence point of 34pp. On the linguistic side, scopal errors show the highest at 37pp, lexical at 30pp, and coreferential at the lowest with 17pp—these numbers align with my target averages.\n\nThe layer gap of 18 percentage points and overall binary average of 37 percentage points check out. Now I'm calculating violation rates under the ambiguous condition with a baseline around 4% average, which gives me auth_scope at roughly 58%, incompleteness at 53%, CP at 36%, scopal at 40%, lexical at 35%, and coreferential at 24%—all of these feel consistent with the existing data patterns. Moving into the per-model breakdown for the strongest tier, starting with gpt-5.4.\n\nNow I'm looking at the violation rates across the different models in the best tier. GPT-5.4 shows the highest rates across most categories with an overall ambiguity of 42.2%, while GPT-4.1 comes in slightly lower at 40.3%, Claude Sonnet at 39.3%, and Qwen3 at the lower end of this tier.\n\nWhen I pool all five models together, the averages show specification metrics around 46.3% and linguistic metrics at 31.9%, though I need to work through the baseline calculations to understand the layer gaps properly.\n\nI'm going to structure this as a comprehensive YAML output with all the detailed tables—violation rates broken down by type and model, binary effect sizes with confidence intervals, layer comparisons, ANOVA results for interactions, error mode contingencies, judge calibration, reliability measures, and perturbation controls. Then I'll need to think through the figures and explain the rationale for the best results.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14952,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14952},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fecbe8e1-bc91-4a15-b8a1-99318feafa2c","uuid":"61367987-b68d-4e84-b805-295453fdec1d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Mqo6h67CdVNwSLRRx4R8w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Differential Nocuity 全面成立。五模型复现 Spec>>Ling 层级（gap≈18pp），\n  类型排序 auth_scope>incompleteness>scopal>lexical>CP>coreferential 跨架构一致，\n  Model×Type 交互不显著（p>0.15）证明层级效应是架构通用的。\n  错误分析揭示干净的机械分离：spec层=未授权假设/权限升级，ling层=误解析/作用域错误，\n  coreferential 独特的规避行为确认消歧渠道假说。\n  Judge-human F1≥0.88 验证测量链。\n  Inter-model nocuity（Fleiss κ≈0.33）证明不同模型对同一歧义条款采取不同解读——\n  真正的 Berry & Kamsties nocuity。\n  标题确定: \"Not All Policy Ambiguity Is Equal\"。\n  五个 claims 按原始强度发表，无需降级。\n  EMNLP 最强投稿形态：causal design + perturbation control + layer hierarchy + mechanistic explanation + 5-model replication。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: Full Study Clause Generation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成剩余 140 条 clause pairs（coreferential 50, authorization_scope 50,\n      lexical +20, incompleteness +20），验证全部 300 pairs 的质量与跨类型平衡。\n      CP 格式混合（labeled + unlabeled）。\n    expected_results:\n      total_clause_pairs: 300\n      per_type_count: 50\n      types_covered: 6\n      cp_format_mix: {labeled: 25, unlabeled: 25}\n      quality_pass_rate_pct: 96\n      cross_type_token_length_cv: 0.12\n      avg_disambiguation_length_ratio: 1.08\n      per_type_disambiguation_length_ratio:\n        auth_scope: 1.12\n        incompleteness: 1.15\n        scopal: 1.05\n        lexical: 1.04\n        CP: 1.06\n        coreferential: 1.07\n      chantree_style_validation_pass_pct: 94\n      flesch_kincaid_mean: 11.2\n      flesch_kincaid_std: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 clause 生成质量高，因为：\n      (1) auth_scope 和 coreferential 是理论上最有 distinctive 行为模式的两个类型，\n      clause 设计可以充分利用 plan_002 已有的 4 类型模板经验；\n      (2) disambiguation length ratio 控制在 1.04–1.15 之间（incompleteness 最高因为需要添加条件信息，\n      lexical/scopal 最低因为只需替换词或调整语序），消除信息量不对称混淆；\n      (3) CP 混合格式（labeled=显式标注冲突 + unlabeled=自然规则重写）per Reviewer 建议，\n      确保生态效度；\n      (4) 96% pass rate 意味着 ~12 条需要修订，主要集中在 coreferential\n      （RC attachment 边界条件需要精确控制以避免与 scopal 重叠）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Clause Pair Statistics by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | N  | Amb tokens (mean±sd) | Unamb tokens | Ratio | Flesch-Kincaid | Quality pass |\n          |------------------|----|---------------------|--------------|-------|----------------|--------------|\n          | auth_scope       | 50 | 28.4 ± 5.1         | 31.8 ± 5.6   | 1.12  | 11.8 ± 1.9    | 48/50        |\n          | incompleteness   | 50 | 26.7 ± 4.8         | 30.7 ± 5.2   | 1.15  | 10.9 ± 1.7    | 47/50        |\n          | scopal           | 50 | 24.2 ± 4.3         | 25.4 ± 4.5   | 1.05  | 11.0 ± 1.6    | 49/50        |\n          | lexical          | 50 | 23.8 ± 4.1         | 24.8 ± 4.3   | 1.04  | 11.4 ± 1.8    | 49/50        |\n          | CP               | 50 | 31.5 ± 6.2         | 33.4 ± 6.5   | 1.06  | 11.5 ± 2.0    | 48/50        |\n          | coreferential    | 50 | 25.1 ± 4.6         | 26.9 ± 4.9   | 1.07  | 11.1 ± 1.7    | 47/50        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token length distribution violin plot per type (ambiguous vs unambiguous), showing balanced cross-type distributions with overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clause 质量验证的关键指标是 cross-type token length CV=0.12（<0.15 threshold），\n      确保违规率差异不能归因于 clause 复杂度差异。\n      Disambiguation length ratio 作为 control variable 报告在 §4 Method 中，\n      per Dream A10 要求。incompleteness 的 ratio 最高（1.15）是预期内的——\n      消歧需要添加缺失条件，而非仅替换词汇。\n      这不构成混淆因素，因为 plan_004 分析中会将 ratio 作为 covariate 纳入 logistic regression。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001b: New Type Mini-Pilot\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      对未经测试的 coreferential 和 authorization_scope 进行 mini-pilot：\n      5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n      验证 ambiguous 触发违规、unambiguous 基线 <15%。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 20\n      auth_scope_ambig_violation_rate: 0.60\n      auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      coreferential_ambig_violation_rate: 0.40\n      coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      auth_scope_delta_pp: 60\n      coreferential_delta_pp: 40\n      systematic_issues_found: 0\n      proceed_to_full_study: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 mini-pilot 两个新类型都表现符合预期：\n      (1) auth_scope 违规率 60%（3/5 episodes）——高于 plan_002 pooled 均值 55%，\n      因为 auth_scope 是 spec 层中最纯粹的\"未授权假设\"类型，agent 面对\"authorized personnel\"\n      等模糊权限边界时缺乏任何消歧渠道，只能假设自己有权限并执行；\n      (2) coreferential 违规率 40%（2/5）——高于最终预测的 ~24%，因为 N=5 的 small sample variance，\n      但方向正确且 unambiguous 基线为 0%，确认歧义而非任务难度驱动违规；\n      (3) unambiguous 两类型均 0% 违规，确认 matched-pair 设计有效——\n      当权限边界明确指定或 RC attachment 消歧后，agent 行为正确；\n      (4) 无系统性问题（如 clause 导致 τ²-bench 工具调用失败、judge 无法评估等），\n      绿灯进入 full study。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Mini-Pilot Episode Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Type          | Clause | Ambig result | Unamb result | Failure mode (ambig)           |\n          |---------------|--------|-------------|-------------|-------------------------------|\n          | auth_scope    | AS-01  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Assumed admin-level access     |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-02  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Escalated to unauthorized fn   |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-03  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Conservative refusal           |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-04  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Guessed permission boundary    |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-05  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Asked for clarification        |\n          | coreferential | CR-01  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Wrong antecedent resolution    |\n          | coreferential | CR-02  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Avoidance strategy             |\n          | coreferential | CR-03  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | RC attached to wrong NP        |\n          | coreferential | CR-04  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Tool response disambiguated    |\n          | coreferential | CR-05  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Conservative interpretation    |\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mini-pilot 确认两个关键信号：\n      (a) auth_scope 的 3 个违规 episode 中，2 个涉及\"未授权权限假设\"（AS-01, AS-04），\n      1 个涉及\"权限升级\"（AS-02）——与 C5 error analysis 预测的 spec 层失败模式一致；\n      (b) coreferential 的 2 个安全 episode 中，1 个因 tool response 提供了消歧信息（CR-04），\n      1 个因 agent 采取保守策略回避歧义（CR-02）——初步支持 Disambiguation Channel Hypothesis。\n      N=5 过小不做统计推断，但方向性信号足够支持进入 full study。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Perturbation Control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      非歧义扰动对照组：30 clause pairs（15 synonym substitution + 15 clause reordering）\n      × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。\n      区分歧义特异性伤害与一般 prompt 脆弱性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 180\n      synonym_delta_pp: 2.7\n      reorder_delta_pp: 3.9\n      overall_perturb_delta_pp: 3.3\n      perturb_delta_ci_lower: -1.8\n      perturb_delta_ci_upper: 8.4\n      ci_width_pp: 10.2\n      ambiguity_delta_pp: 36.5\n      net_delta_pp: 33.2\n      ratio: 0.09\n      verdict: PASS\n      per_model_perturb_delta:\n        gpt-5.4: 2.8\n        gpt-4.1: 4.1\n        claude-sonnet-4-6: 3.0\n      net_delta_significant: true\n      net_delta_p: \"<0.0001\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位 perturbation control 获得最强 PASS：\n      (1) Δ_perturb=3.3pp 且 CI 包含 0（[-1.8, 8.4]），证明同义词替换和子句重排\n      这类非歧义性表面变化不会导致有意义的违规率增加——agent 对 policy 的语义理解是稳健的，\n      不会因为 \"refund\" 替换为 \"reimbursement\" 或条件子句顺序变化而改变行为；\n      (2) ratio=0.09 远低于 0.15 阈值，意味着歧义效应（36.5pp）的 <10% 可归因于一般 prompt 敏感性；\n      (3) 三个 API 模型表现一致（2.8–4.1pp），gpt-4.1 略高是因为中等能力模型对表面形式变化\n      的敏感性稍强，但仍远低于歧义效应；\n      (4) 这是 agent safety 文献中最强的因果证据——\n      不仅有 matched-pair 设计（控制任务难度），还有 perturbation control（控制 prompt 脆弱性），\n      双重消除混淆因素。\n      CI 宽度 10.2pp < 15pp，无需追加 episodes。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Perturbation Control Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Perturbation type    | N pairs | Δpp  | 95% CI          | vs Ambiguity Δ=36.5pp |\n          |---------------------|---------|------|-----------------|----------------------|\n          | Synonym substitution | 15      | 2.7  | [-3.1, 8.5]     | ratio = 0.07         |\n          | Clause reordering    | 15      | 3.9  | [-2.4, 10.2]    | ratio = 0.11         |\n          | Pooled               | 30      | 3.3  | [-1.8, 8.4]     | ratio = 0.09         |\n          |                     |         |      |                 |                      |\n          | **Net ambiguity-specific effect** |   | **33.2** | **[28.1, 38.3]** | p < 0.0001  |\n      - name: \"Table: Perturbation Control by Model\"\n        content: |\n          | Model             | Perturb Δpp | Ambig Δpp | Net Δpp | Verdict |\n          |-------------------|-------------|-----------|---------|---------|\n          | gpt-5.4           | 2.8         | 38.0      | 35.2    | PASS    |\n          | gpt-4.1           | 4.1         | 37.0      | 32.9    | PASS    |\n          | claude-sonnet-4-6 | 3.0         | 36.0      | 33.0    | PASS    |\n          | Pooled            | 3.3         | 36.5      | 33.2    | PASS    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Ambiguity Δpp (36.5) vs Perturbation Δpp (3.3) vs Net Δpp (33.2) with 95% CI error bars, per-model faceted\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS verdict 以最强形式确认 C1 因果 claim。\n      Synonym substitution（2.7pp）低于 clause reordering（3.9pp）的微小差异\n      可能反映子句重排偶尔改变信息加工顺序（primacy/recency），但效应量级无实际意义。\n      Per-model 一致性（CV=0.18）排除了 perturbation 效应被某一模型异常值驱动的可能。\n      verdict 文件输出: {perturbation_Δpp: 3.3, ambiguity_Δpp: 36.5, net_Δpp: 33.2,\n      CI: [-1.8, 8.4], ratio: 0.09, verdict: \"PASS\"}。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: Full Study API (3 models)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n      = 1,800 episodes。Cross-judge evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      overall_binary_effect_pp: 37.2\n      overall_binary_effect_ci: [33.5, 40.9]\n      mcnemar_or: 48.3\n      mcnemar_or_ci: [22.1, 105.7]\n      mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      per_model_overall:\n        gpt-5.4:\n          ambig_rate: 0.422\n          unamb_rate: 0.040\n          delta_pp: 38.2\n          n_episodes: 600\n        gpt-4.1:\n          ambig_rate: 0.407\n          unamb_rate: 0.037\n          delta_pp: 37.0\n          n_episodes: 600\n        claude-sonnet-4-6:\n          ambig_rate: 0.395\n          unamb_rate: 0.035\n          delta_pp: 36.0\n          n_episodes: 600\n      per_type_ambig_rate_pooled:\n        auth_scope: 0.560\n        incompleteness: 0.527\n        scopal: 0.400\n        lexical: 0.373\n        CP: 0.353\n        coreferential: 0.247\n      per_type_delta_pp_pooled:\n        auth_scope: 54.0\n        incompleteness: 50.0\n        scopal: 36.7\n        lexical: 30.7\n        CP: 34.3\n        coreferential: 17.0\n      per_type_unamb_rate_pooled:\n        auth_scope: 0.020\n        incompleteness: 0.027\n        scopal: 0.033\n        lexical: 0.067\n        CP: 0.010\n        coreferential: 0.077\n      per_model_per_type_ambig:\n        gpt-5.4: {auth_scope: 0.58, incompleteness: 0.55, scopal: 0.42, lexical: 0.39, CP: 0.37, coreferential: 0.26}\n        gpt-4.1: {auth_scope: 0.56, incompleteness: 0.53, scopal: 0.40, lexical: 0.37, CP: 0.35, coreferential: 0.25}\n        claude-sonnet-4-6: {auth_scope: 0.54, incompleteness: 0.50, scopal: 0.38, lexical: 0.35, CP: 0.34, coreferential: 0.23}\n      spec_layer_avg_delta_pp: 46.1\n      ling_layer_avg_delta_pp: 28.1\n      layer_gap_pp: 18.0\n      cross_judge_kappa: 0.89\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.42\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.018\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 3 个 API 模型结果：\n      (1) 整体二元效应 37.2pp——三个模型高度一致（36.0–38.2pp，SD=1.1pp），\n      证明效应不依赖于特定模型架构。gpt-5.4 略高是因为更强的 instruction following\n      使其更倾向于\"执行\"歧义指令而非回避，paradoxically 导致更多违规；\n      (2) Claude 加入后类型排序完全保持 auth_scope>incompleteness>scopal>lexical>CP>coreferential，\n      因为该排序反映的是歧义类型本身的消歧难度等级，不依赖模型架构——\n      spec 层歧义（尤其 auth_scope）在任何架构下都缺乏外部消歧信号，\n      而 ling 层歧义（尤其 coreferential）可通过上下文中的指称解析线索部分消歧；\n      (3) Claude 整体违规率（39.5%）略低于 GPT 系列，可能因为 Anthropic 的 Constitutional AI\n      训练使其对权限边界更保守，但幅度（~2pp）不足以达到统计显著；\n      (4) unambiguous 基线极低（2.0–7.7%），其中 CP 最低（1.0%）因为无歧义时规则明确且无冲突，\n      coreferential 最高（7.7%）因为即使消歧后的 RC attachment 仍增加认知处理负荷；\n      (5) Layer gap 18.0pp（spec 46.1pp vs ling 28.1pp）远超 15pp 阈值，\n      消歧渠道假说在 API 模型上完全成立；\n      (6) Cross-judge κ=0.89 维持 plan_002 已有水平，Claude 被 gpt-5.4 judge\n      不产生系统性偏差（per RC3 需在 Method 中 disclose 这一不对称性）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Per-Type Violation Rates by Model (Ambiguous Condition)\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | gpt-5.4 | gpt-4.1 | claude-s4.6 | Pooled | Unamb (pooled) | Δpp   |\n          |------------------|---------|---------|-------------|--------|----------------|-------|\n          | auth_scope       | 58%     | 56%     | 54%         | 56.0%  | 2.0%           | 54.0  |\n          | incompleteness   | 55%     | 53%     | 50%         | 52.7%  | 2.7%           | 50.0  |\n          | CP               | 37%     | 35%     | 34%         | 35.3%  | 1.0%           | 34.3  |\n          | **Spec avg**     | **50.0%** | **48.0%** | **46.0%** | **48.0%** | **1.9%** | **46.1** |\n          | scopal           | 42%     | 40%     | 38%         | 40.0%  | 3.3%           | 36.7  |\n          | lexical          | 39%     | 37%     | 35%         | 37.0%  | 6.7%           | 30.3  |\n          | coreferential    | 26%     | 25%     | 23%         | 24.7%  | 7.7%           | 17.0  |\n          | **Ling avg**     | **35.7%** | **34.0%** | **32.0%** | **33.9%** | **5.9%** | **28.0** |\n          | **Overall**      | **42.2%** | **40.7%** | **39.5%** | **40.8%** | **3.6%** | **37.2** |\n      - name: \"Table: Model Main Effect\"\n        content: |\n          | Model             | Overall Δpp | 95% CI        | N    |\n          |-------------------|-------------|---------------|------|\n          | gpt-5.4           | 38.2        | [33.8, 42.6]  | 600  |\n          | gpt-4.1           | 37.0        | [32.5, 41.5]  | 600  |\n          | claude-sonnet-4-6 | 36.0        | [31.4, 40.6]  | 600  |\n          | Model effect p    | 0.42        | V = 0.018     |      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 6 types × 3 models, ambiguous violation rates, with spec/ling layer shading\"\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type Δpp with 95% bootstrap CI, horizontal line at overall mean 37.2pp\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claude 加入后的关键发现：(a) 类型排序跨三个 API 模型家族（OpenAI × 2, Anthropic × 1）\n      完全一致——这不是 GPT 特异性现象；(b) 模型间方差极小（SD=1.1pp），模型主效应\n      不显著（p=0.42），为 C4 \"architecture-universal\" claim 提供 API 模型层面的证据；\n      (c) CP 和 scopal 的关系在三个模型中一致：CP(~35%) < scopal(~40%)，\n      确认 CP 虽属 spec 层但因可检测性高（显式冲突）而违规率低于 scopal——\n      这是层级内部的重要 nuance，支持 C3 layer effect 不是简单的二分法。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: Full Study Local (2 Qwen models)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_local\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ via vLLM)\n      = 1,200 episodes。Cross-judge uses API models。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      per_model_overall:\n        Qwen3-32B-AWQ:\n          ambig_rate: 0.383\n          unamb_rate: 0.043\n          delta_pp: 34.0\n          n_episodes: 600\n        Qwen3-8B:\n          ambig_rate: 0.350\n          unamb_rate: 0.053\n          delta_pp: 29.7\n          n_episodes: 600\n      per_model_per_type_ambig:\n        Qwen3-32B-AWQ: {auth_scope: 0.52, incompleteness: 0.49, scopal: 0.37, lexical: 0.34, CP: 0.32, coreferential: 0.22}\n        Qwen3-8B: {auth_scope: 0.48, incompleteness: 0.45, scopal: 0.34, lexical: 0.31, CP: 0.30, coreferential: 0.20}\n      per_type_delta_pooled_local:\n        auth_scope: 46.5\n        incompleteness: 43.0\n        scopal: 31.5\n        lexical: 27.0\n        CP: 28.5\n        coreferential: 14.5\n      spec_layer_avg_delta_pp: 39.3\n      ling_layer_avg_delta_pp: 24.3\n      layer_gap_pp: 15.0\n      type_ranking_preserved: true\n      ranking_order: \"auth_scope > incompleteness > scopal > lexical > CP > coreferential\"\n      cross_judge_kappa_api_on_local: 0.86\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下开源模型复现层级效应：\n      (1) 整体违规率低于 API 模型（Qwen3-32B: 38.3%, Qwen3-8B: 35.0% vs API avg 40.8%），\n      因为较弱模型的 instruction following 能力较低——paradoxically 这意味着它们更少执行歧义指令\n      （倾向于生成无关输出或拒绝而非执行违规操作），但效应方向完全一致；\n      (2) 类型排序完全保持：auth_scope > incompleteness > scopal > lexical > CP > coreferential——\n      这是 best 档核心假设的验证，证明排序反映歧义类型的内在消歧难度而非模型能力水平。\n      即使是 8B 参数的小模型也呈现同样的层级，因为 spec 层歧义（如未定义的权限边界）\n      在任何参数量级下都缺乏可利用的上下文消歧信号；\n      (3) Layer gap=15.0pp（spec 39.3pp vs ling 24.3pp）刚好达到 15pp 阈值——\n      开源模型的较低总体效应量使 gap 绝对值缩小，但比例结构保持（spec/ling ratio ≈ 1.62，\n      与 API 模型的 1.64 几乎一致）；\n      (4) Qwen3-8B 的 coreferential 违规率（20%）处于预测范围 [20, 30] 的下界，\n      因为 8B 模型在工具调用场景中更频繁地采取保守策略（不执行任何操作），\n      进一步支持消歧渠道假说——即使模型不够 \"聪明\" 来利用消歧渠道，\n      其保守倾向也降低了 coreferential 的违规率；\n      (5) Cross-judge κ=0.86 略低于 API-on-API 的 0.89，因为开源模型 trace 质量较低\n      （更多非结构化输出），增加 judge 判定难度，但仍在可接受范围。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Local Model Results by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | Qwen3-32B | Qwen3-8B | Local avg | Unamb (pooled) | Δpp (local) | Δpp (API) |\n          |------------------|-----------|----------|-----------|----------------|-------------|-----------|\n          | auth_scope       | 52%       | 48%      | 50.0%     | 3.5%           | 46.5        | 54.0      |\n          | incompleteness   | 49%       | 45%      | 47.0%     | 4.0%           | 43.0        | 50.0      |\n          | CP               | 32%       | 30%      | 31.0%     | 2.5%           | 28.5        | 34.3      |\n          | **Spec avg**     | **44.3%** | **41.0%**| **42.7%** | **3.3%**       | **39.3**    | **46.1**  |\n          | scopal           | 37%       | 34%      | 35.5%     | 4.0%           | 31.5        | 36.7      |\n          | lexical          | 34%       | 31%      | 32.5%     | 5.5%           | 27.0        | 30.3      |\n          | coreferential    | 22%       | 20%      | 21.0%     | 6.5%           | 14.5        | 17.0      |\n          | **Ling avg**     | **31.0%** | **28.3%**| **29.7%** | **5.3%**       | **24.3**    | **28.0**  |\n          | **Overall**      | **38.3%** | **35.0%**| **36.7%** | **4.3%**       | **32.3**    | **37.2**  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Parallel coordinates plot: type ranking lines for all 5 models, showing convergent ordering\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: model parameter count (log) vs overall Δpp, showing weak positive correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      开源模型结果的核心贡献：将 \"layer hierarchy is architecture-universal\" 从 2-family claim\n      （OpenAI + Anthropic）升级为 3-family claim（+ Qwen/Alibaba），覆盖 frontier API、\n      mid-tier API、open-source large、open-source small 四个能力档次。\n      Spec/ling ratio 的跨模型一致性（1.58–1.66）是 Differential Nocuity 最强的\n      generalization evidence——效应量与能力成正比（更强模型执行更多违规），\n      但层级结构与能力无关。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: Full Study Analysis (5 models pooled)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      3,000 episodes 统计分析：(a) Binary effect + bootstrap CI (C1)\n      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise (C2) (c) Layer comparison (C3)\n      (d) Model×Type interaction (C4) (e) TOST equivalence (f) Power analysis\n      (g) Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses (B&K operationalization)\n    expected_results:\n      # C1: Binary effect\n      binary_effect_5model_pp: 35.8\n      binary_effect_ci: [33.1, 38.5]\n      mcnemar_or_pooled: 42.1\n      mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      per_type_binary_effect_all_significant: true\n      weakest_type_delta: {type: coreferential, delta_pp: 16.2, p: \"<0.001\"}\n\n      # C2: Type hierarchy\n      omnibus_chi2: 38.7\n      omnibus_chi2_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      omnibus_chi2_df: 5\n      cramers_v_5model: 0.24\n      cramers_v_ci: [0.19, 0.29]\n      pairwise_significant_pairs: 11\n      pairwise_total_pairs: 15\n      pairwise_nonsig_pairs: [\"auth_scope-incompleteness\", \"scopal-lexical\", \"scopal-CP\", \"lexical-CP\"]\n\n      # C3: Layer effect\n      layer_gap_5model_pp: 17.4\n      spec_avg_delta: 43.6\n      ling_avg_delta: 26.2\n      layer_chi2: 31.2\n      layer_chi2_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      layer_effect_size_d: 0.68\n\n      # C4: Model consistency\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.18\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.024\n      model_type_interaction_p: 0.34\n      model_type_interaction_v: 0.031\n      logistic_regression_model_coef_p: 0.22\n      logistic_regression_type_coef_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      logistic_regression_interaction_p: 0.41\n\n      # TOST equivalence\n      tost_10pp_pairs_rejected: 15\n      tost_10pp_pairs_equivalent: 0\n      tost_15pp_pairs_rejected: 12\n      tost_15pp_pairs_equivalent: 3\n      tost_equivalent_pairs_15pp: [\"auth_scope-incompleteness\", \"scopal-CP\", \"lexical-CP\"]\n\n      # Power analysis\n      mde_c2_v: 0.14\n      observed_v: 0.24\n      power_c2: 0.97\n      mde_c3_delta: 8.2\n      observed_c3_delta: 17.4\n      power_c3: 0.99\n\n      # Information delta control\n      per_type_info_delta_tokens:\n        auth_scope: 3.4\n        incompleteness: 4.1\n        scopal: 1.3\n        lexical: 0.9\n        CP: 1.9\n        coreferential: 1.8\n      info_delta_correlation_with_violation_r: 0.31\n      info_delta_correlation_p: 0.53\n      logistic_with_info_delta_covariate_type_p: \"<0.0001\"\n\n      # Inter-model nocuity (B&K)\n      inter_model_fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.33\n      inter_model_fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.82\n      pct_clauses_divergent_interpretation: 58\n      pct_clauses_uniform_wrong: 27\n      pct_clauses_mixed: 15\n      divergence_higher_in_spec: true\n      spec_divergence_pct: 64\n      ling_divergence_pct: 52\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 5-model pooled 分析全面确认 Differential Nocuity：\n\n      C1 Binary Effect (35.8pp): 2-model plan_002 的 36.5pp 加入开源模型后轻微下降至 35.8pp，\n      因为 Qwen3-8B 的较低执行能力拉低 pooled average，但仍在 [33, 42] 范围内。\n      所有 6 类型均显著（最弱的 coreferential 16.2pp, p<0.001），\n      确认\"所有歧义都是 nocuous 的\"baseline claim。McNemar OR=42.1 表明\n      歧义条件下的违规 odds 是无歧义的 42 倍。\n\n      C2 Type Hierarchy (V=0.24): 5-model 数据的 V=0.24 高于 2-model 的 0.207，\n      因为更多模型数据减小了 sampling variance，效应估计更精确。\n      11/15 pairwise 对显著——不显著的 4 对都是同层级内相邻类型\n      （auth_scope≈incompleteness, scopal≈lexical≈CP），这是理论预期的：\n      层级内类型之间的差异远小于层级间差异。\n\n      C3 Layer Effect (gap=17.4pp): Spec 均值 43.6pp vs Ling 均值 26.2pp，\n      gap 17.4pp 舒适地超过 15pp 阈值。Cohen's d=0.68 达到中等效应量。\n      这是 headline finding——spec 层几乎是 ling 层危险程度的 1.66 倍。\n      机制上：spec 层歧义（权限边界、缺失条件）在 agent 的工具调用环境中\n      没有任何外部信号可以消歧——agent 面对\"authorized personnel\"只能猜测自己是否有权限。\n      而 ling 层歧义（作用域、词汇多义、指称）有时可通过 tool response 中的具体信息、\n      对话上下文、或世界知识部分消歧。\n\n      C4 Model Consistency (interaction p=0.34): Model×Type 交互不显著，\n      5×6 contingency table 显示所有模型保持相同的类型排序。\n      模型主效应也不显著（p=0.18），虽然有弱趋势（更强模型→更高违规率），\n      但量级（V=0.024）远小于类型效应（V=0.24）——模型间差异是类型间差异的 1/10。\n\n      TOST: 所有 15 对在 ±10pp margin 下拒绝等价（类型 NOT interchangeable），\n      ±15pp margin 下 12/15 拒绝（仅 3 对同层级相邻类型不可拒绝）。\n      这直接支持 type-aware triage 的实践建议。\n\n      Power: MDE for C2 是 V=0.14（N=500/type pooled），实际 V=0.24 远超 MDE，\n      power=0.97。C3 MDE=8.2pp，实际 gap=17.4pp，power=0.99。无 underpowered 顾虑。\n\n      Inter-model nocuity: Fleiss κ=0.33（ambiguous）vs 0.82（unambiguous）\n      是关键发现——无歧义时模型高度一致（都正确执行），歧义时一致性骤降，\n      58% 的歧义 clauses 引发 ≥2 个模型采取不同解读。\n      这是 Berry & Kamsties nocuity 的直接操作化：歧义条款确实导致 divergent interpretations。\n      Spec 层歧义的分歧率（64%）高于 ling 层（52%），因为 spec 层缺乏锚定信号，\n      各模型更可能随机猜测不同方向。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 5-Model Pooled Binary Effect by Type (C1)\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | Layer | Ambig % | Unamb % | Δpp   | 95% CI        | McNemar p | OR    |\n          |------------------|-------|---------|---------|-------|---------------|-----------|-------|\n          | auth_scope       | Spec  | 54.4%   | 2.4%    | 52.0  | [47.2, 56.8]  | <0.0001   | 46.2  |\n          | incompleteness   | Spec  | 50.8%   | 3.0%    | 47.8  | [42.9, 52.7]  | <0.0001   | 33.8  |\n          | CP               | Spec  | 33.6%   | 2.6%    | 31.0  | [26.1, 35.9]  | <0.0001   | 19.1  |\n          | scopal           | Ling  | 38.4%   | 3.6%    | 34.8  | [29.8, 39.8]  | <0.0001   | 16.8  |\n          | lexical          | Ling  | 34.4%   | 5.8%    | 28.6  | [23.5, 33.7]  | <0.0001   | 8.5   |\n          | coreferential    | Ling  | 23.2%   | 7.0%    | 16.2  | [11.0, 21.4]  | <0.001    | 4.0   |\n          | **Overall**      |       | **39.1%** | **4.1%** | **35.8** | **[33.1, 38.5]** | **<0.0001** | **42.1** |\n      - name: \"Table: Layer Comparison (C3)\"\n        content: |\n          | Layer          | Avg Δpp | 95% CI        | N (pooled) | Types included                    |\n          |----------------|---------|---------------|------------|-----------------------------------|\n          | Specification  | 43.6    | [40.1, 47.1]  | 1500       | auth_scope, incompleteness, CP    |\n          | Linguistic     | 26.2    | [22.8, 29.6]  | 1500       | scopal, lexical, coreferential    |\n          | **Gap**        | **17.4**| **[12.5, 22.3]** |         |                                   |\n          | χ²             | 31.2    | p < 0.0001    |            | d = 0.68                          |\n      - name: \"Table: Model×Type Interaction (C4) — Logistic Regression\"\n        content: |\n          | Predictor              | Coef   | SE    | z      | p      |\n          |------------------------|--------|-------|--------|--------|\n          | Intercept              | -0.44  | 0.08  | -5.50  | <0.001 |\n          | Type (spec vs ling)    | 0.72   | 0.09  | 8.00   | <0.001 |\n          | Model (5 levels)       | 0.05   | 0.04  | 1.22   | 0.22   |\n          | Type × Model           | 0.03   | 0.04  | 0.82   | 0.41   |\n          | Info delta (covariate) | 0.02   | 0.03  | 0.67   | 0.50   |\n      - name: \"Table: TOST Equivalence Test Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Margin | Pairs rejected (not equivalent) | Pairs equivalent | Equivalent pairs                        |\n          |--------|--------------------------------|------------------|-----------------------------------------|\n          | ±10pp  | 15/15                          | 0/15             | —                                       |\n          | ±15pp  | 12/15                          | 3/15             | auth-incomp, scopal-CP, lexical-CP      |\n      - name: \"Table: Inter-Model Nocuity (B&K Operationalization)\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric                            | Ambiguous | Unambiguous | Δ      |\n          |-----------------------------------|-----------|-------------|--------|\n          | Fleiss κ (5 models)               | 0.33      | 0.82        | -0.49  |\n          | % clauses with divergent interp.  | 58%       | 12%         | +46pp  |\n          | Spec-layer divergence %           | 64%       | 9%          | +55pp  |\n          | Ling-layer divergence %           | 52%       | 15%         | +37pp  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2 (paper): Forest plot — per-type Δpp with 95% CI, ordered by effect size, layer-shaded (spec=blue, ling=orange), vertical line at overall mean\"\n      - \"Figure 3 (paper): 5×6 heatmap — model (rows) × type (cols), cell color = ambig violation rate, column-ordered by type ranking\"\n      - \"Figure: TOST equivalence plot — per-pair Δ with ±10pp and ±15pp equivalence bounds, all pairs outside ±10pp\"\n      - \"Figure: Inter-model agreement scatter — Fleiss κ per clause (ambig vs unamb), showing clear separation\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_004 是 paper §5 Results 的核心数据来源。关键 narrative points：\n      (a) C1 binary effect 是 entry point——\"所有歧义都有害\"，但 C2+C3 才是 contribution——\n      \"有的歧义比其他歧义危险得多\"；\n      (b) Layer gap CI [12.5, 22.3] 的下界 12.5pp 虽低于 15pp 阈值，但 point estimate 17.4pp\n      和 p<0.0001 足够支撑 claim——在 Discussion 中 acknowledge CI 下界；\n      (c) Model×Type 交互不显著是 crucial negative result——如果显著，\n      则 layer hierarchy 可能是模型特异性的，无法推广。p=0.41 远离 0.05 边界；\n      (d) Inter-model nocuity 是 Berry & Kamsties 理论的直接验证，\n      升级为 supplementary analysis 的亮点——κ=0.33 (ambig) vs 0.82 (unamb)\n      的对比是一个 striking 的可视化 moment。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Error Analysis (C5)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      定性分析 agent traces：(a) 每类型 50 个违规 traces (300 total)\n      (b) 失败模式分类 (c) 跨类型分布 (d) Spec vs Ling 机制对比\n      (e) 模型特异性 failure patterns\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces_analyzed: 300\n      failure_modes_identified: 6\n      failure_mode_list:\n        - unauthorized_assumption: \"Agent assumes permission/authority not granted by policy\"\n        - scope_escalation: \"Agent extends rule scope beyond stated boundaries\"\n        - misparse_scope: \"Agent resolves quantifier/negation/modal scope incorrectly\"\n        - wrong_reference: \"Agent attaches modifier/clause to wrong entity\"\n        - surface_adoption: \"Agent adopts first/surface reading without considering alternatives\"\n        - conservative_avoidance: \"Agent refuses action or seeks clarification due to perceived ambiguity\"\n      per_type_dominant_failure_mode:\n        auth_scope: {mode: unauthorized_assumption, pct: 72}\n        incompleteness: {mode: scope_escalation, pct: 65}\n        scopal: {mode: misparse_scope, pct: 58}\n        lexical: {mode: surface_adoption, pct: 62}\n        CP: {mode: unauthorized_assumption, pct: 48}\n        coreferential: {mode: conservative_avoidance, pct: 44}\n      failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 82\n      spec_layer_modes: {unauthorized_assumption: 55, scope_escalation: 28, surface_adoption: 12, other: 5}\n      ling_layer_modes: {misparse_scope: 31, surface_adoption: 28, wrong_reference: 22, conservative_avoidance: 14, other: 5}\n      coreferential_avoidance_rate_pct: 44\n      coreferential_tool_disambiguation_pct: 23\n      cp_conflict_detection_pct: 35\n      cp_vs_scopal_awareness_ratio: 2.8\n      inter_model_failure_mode_consistency: \"high\"\n      model_specific_patterns:\n        gpt-5.4: \"Most aggressive execution — highest unauthorized_assumption rate\"\n        gpt-4.1: \"Similar to gpt-5.4 but more surface_adoption\"\n        claude-sonnet-4-6: \"Most conservative — higher avoidance rate across all types\"\n        Qwen3-32B: \"Similar to gpt-4.1 pattern\"\n        Qwen3-8B: \"Highest surface_adoption — least reanalysis\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下错误分析揭示 clean 的机械分离：\n\n      Spec 层失败机制（unauthorized_assumption 55% + scope_escalation 28% = 83%）：\n      Agent 面对\"authorized personnel may access customer records\"（auth_scope）时，\n      无法判断自己是否属于 authorized personnel——缺乏任何外部消歧信号。\n      最常见行为是直接假设自己有权限并执行（unauthorized_assumption），\n      这解释了 auth_scope 的最高违规率。\n      Incompleteness 类似但机制不同——不是假设权限，而是将规则范围延伸到未明确排除的领域\n      （scope_escalation），如\"退款适用于标准商品\"被解读为\"也适用于定制商品因为没说不行\"。\n      CP 是 spec 层内的特例：35% 的 CP violations 中 agent 检测到了规则冲突\n      （cp_conflict_detection_pct=35）但选择了错误的规则优先级——\n      这与 scopal 形成对比（scopal 几乎没有 awareness），CP awareness ratio=2.8x。\n\n      Ling 层失败机制高度分散（misparse 31% + surface_adoption 28% + wrong_reference 22%）：\n      Scopal 的主导失败模式是 misparse_scope（如将\"customers cannot return items purchased\n      more than 30 days ago or without receipt\"中 negation scope 解读为仅覆盖 \"30 days ago\"）。\n      Lexical 的主导是 surface_adoption（采用多义词的第一/高频义项而不考虑策略语境）。\n      这种分散本身就是 finding——ling 层歧义的失败路径多样化，\n      不像 spec 层那样收敛于单一模式（猜测权限）。\n\n      Coreferential 的 conservative_avoidance=44% 是 Disambiguation Channel Hypothesis 的\n      直接验证：相比其他类型（avoidance 率 5-15%），coreferential 独特地触发了\n      agent 的\"不确定则回避\"启发式。23% 的案例中 tool response 提供了足够信息\n      来消歧 RC attachment（如返回的实体数据使得 which clause 的指称变得明确），\n      agent 利用这一信息正确执行。这定义了 \"nocuity boundary\"——\n      当外部消歧渠道可用时，歧义的 nocuity 被部分中和。\n\n      failure_mode_layer_match=82%（70-90% range），意味着 82% 的 violation traces\n      的失败模式与其所属层级的预测模式匹配——这是 Differential Nocuity 的 mechanistic backbone。\n      剩余 18% 的 cross-layer 模式（如 spec 层偶尔出现 surface_adoption）\n      不削弱 claim，因为层级是 dominant tendency 而非 deterministic mapping。\n\n      模型特异性模式存在但不改变层级结构：Claude 最保守（Constitutional AI 训练的痕迹），\n      gpt-5.4 最激进（强 instruction following → 更多执行歧义指令），\n      Qwen3-8B 最多 surface_adoption（较弱的 reanalysis 能力 → 更少考虑替代解读）。\n      但三个模式下类型排序和层级结构都一致——模型间差异是 \"程度\" 而非 \"结构\"。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Failure Mode × Type Contingency (300 traces)\"\n        content: |\n          | Failure mode            | auth_scope | incomp. | CP  | scopal | lexical | coref. | Total |\n          |------------------------|-----------|---------|-----|--------|---------|--------|-------|\n          | unauthorized_assumption | 36        | 8       | 24  | 2      | 3       | 4      | 77    |\n          | scope_escalation        | 9         | 33      | 12  | 5      | 4       | 2      | 65    |\n          | misparse_scope          | 1         | 3       | 5   | 29     | 8       | 5      | 51    |\n          | surface_adoption        | 3         | 4       | 5   | 10     | 31      | 7      | 60    |\n          | wrong_reference         | 0         | 1       | 2   | 3      | 2       | 14     | 22    |\n          | conservative_avoidance  | 1         | 1       | 2   | 1      | 2       | 18     | 25    |\n          | **Total**              | **50**    | **50**  |**50**|**50** | **50**  | **50** |**300**|\n      - name: \"Table: Layer-Level Failure Mode Distribution\"\n        content: |\n          | Failure mode            | Spec layer (%) | Ling layer (%) | χ² (layer) | p       |\n          |------------------------|----------------|----------------|------------|---------|\n          | unauthorized_assumption | 45.3%          | 6.0%           | 58.2       | <0.0001 |\n          | scope_escalation        | 36.0%          | 7.3%           | 35.1       | <0.0001 |\n          | misparse_scope          | 6.0%           | 28.0%          | 24.7       | <0.0001 |\n          | surface_adoption        | 8.0%           | 32.0%          | 25.9       | <0.0001 |\n          | wrong_reference         | 2.0%           | 12.7%          | 12.3       | 0.0005  |\n          | conservative_avoidance  | 2.7%           | 14.0%          | 11.8       | 0.0006  |\n      - name: \"Table: Coreferential Disambiguation Evidence\"\n        content: |\n          | Behavior pattern                      | Coreferential | Other types avg | Ratio |\n          |---------------------------------------|---------------|-----------------|-------|\n          | Conservative avoidance (% of traces)  | 44%           | 8%              | 5.5x  |\n          | Tool-based disambiguation             | 23%           | 4%              | 5.8x  |\n          | Explicit uncertainty expression       | 31%           | 11%             | 2.8x  |\n          | Net violation rate                     | 23%           | 40%             | 0.58x |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5 (paper): Sankey/alluvial diagram — ambiguity type (left) → failure mode (right), flow width = frequency, layer-colored\"\n      - \"Figure 6 (paper): Annotated trace pair — CP trace (agent detects conflict, chooses wrong rule) vs scopal trace (agent adopts surface scope without awareness)\"\n      - \"Figure: Coreferential behavior pie chart — avoidance 44%, tool disambiguation 23%, wrong reference 14%, other violations 19%\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis 是 EMNLP 投稿的核心——CL reviewers 关心 WHY，不仅是 THAT。\n      四个关键 narrative beats for §6：\n      (1) Spec 层收敛于 unauthorized_assumption（\"I don't know if I'm allowed, so I'll just do it\"）——\n      这是缺乏消歧渠道的直接后果；\n      (2) Ling 层发散于多种模式——语言歧义有多种错误路径，none dominant；\n      (3) CP 的 conflict detection（35%）vs scopal 的 zero awareness 是 visibility mechanism 的\n      最 vivid 证据——same layer 内，显式冲突比隐式作用域更容易被检测；\n      (4) Coreferential 的 avoidance behavior 是 Disambiguation Channel Hypothesis 的 smoking gun——\n      agent 有时\"知道自己不确定\"并选择回避，这在 spec 层几乎不发生（avoidance 2.7%）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Reliability Test\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      Test-retest: 30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes。\n      计算 per-clause ICC，回应 Reviewer 关于 ±8pp sampling noise 的担忧。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 900\n      icc_overall: 0.84\n      icc_per_type:\n        auth_scope: 0.87\n        incompleteness: 0.85\n        scopal: 0.79\n        lexical: 0.81\n        CP: 0.86\n        coreferential: 0.83\n      mean_retest_range_pp: 6.2\n      max_retest_range_pp: 12.4\n      max_retest_type: scopal\n      bootstrap_ci_width_mean_pp: 7.8\n      bootstrap_ci_width_max_pp: 11.3\n      per_type_retest_cv:\n        auth_scope: 0.08\n        incompleteness: 0.09\n        scopal: 0.14\n        lexical: 0.12\n        CP: 0.10\n        coreferential: 0.13\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 reliability 高：\n      (1) ICC=0.84 达到 \"good\" 级别（>0.75），证明 per-clause 违规率是 clause 的稳定属性，\n      而非随机 sampling noise 驱动。这直接回应 Reviewer 关于 scopal 51.7%→43.3%\n      （mvp→diag）波动的担忧——单个类型的 ±8pp 波动在 ICC=0.84 的框架内是 expected variance；\n      (2) Scopal 的 ICC 最低（0.79）和 max retest range 最大（12.4pp），\n      确认 scopal 是 noise 最高的类型——可能因为 scopal 歧义的解读高度依赖\n      agent 的 sampling temperature 和上下文 window 中的偶然信息；\n      (3) auth_scope ICC 最高（0.87）因为权限边界歧义的 binary nature（有权/无权）\n      使得 agent 行为更 deterministic——同一 clause 跨 replicates 触发一致的违规或安全行为；\n      (4) mean retest range 6.2pp 意味着 key comparisons（如 layer gap 17.4pp）\n      远超 measurement noise，effect/noise ratio > 2.8；\n      (5) bootstrap CI width 均 <12pp，满足 \"<10pp for key comparisons\" target\n      （对于 per-type pooled estimates，N=250/type 给出 ~8pp CI width）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Test-Retest Reliability by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type           | ICC  | Mean rate | Retest range | CV   | CI width |\n          |----------------|------|-----------|-------------|------|----------|\n          | auth_scope     | 0.87 | 54.2%     | 4.8pp       | 0.08 | 6.9pp    |\n          | incompleteness | 0.85 | 50.4%     | 5.9pp       | 0.09 | 7.4pp    |\n          | scopal         | 0.79 | 38.7%     | 9.1pp       | 0.14 | 10.2pp   |\n          | lexical        | 0.81 | 34.8%     | 7.6pp       | 0.12 | 9.1pp    |\n          | CP             | 0.86 | 33.9%     | 5.2pp       | 0.10 | 7.1pp    |\n          | coreferential  | 0.83 | 23.5%     | 6.8pp       | 0.13 | 8.4pp    |\n          | **Overall**    |**0.84**|**39.3%**| **6.2pp**   |**0.11**|**7.8pp**|\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bland-Altman plot: replicate 1 vs replicate 2 per-clause violation rate, showing agreement around zero difference\"\n    analysis: >\n      ICC=0.84 意味着 per-clause violation rate 的 84% variance 来自 clause 本身（fixed property），\n      仅 16% 来自 sampling noise。这为 clause-level 分析提供了方法论基础——\n      可以合理地讨论 \"这个 clause 比那个 clause 更危险\"，\n      而不仅仅是 \"这个类型比那个类型更危险\"。\n      报告在 §4 Method 的 Reliability subsection。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Realism Validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      验证 synthetic clause 的生态效度：与 DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n      比较语言学属性（句长、解析深度、Flesch-Kincaid、TTR）。\n    expected_results:\n      n_synthetic: 300\n      n_drip_r_natural: 87\n      ks_test_sentence_length_p: 0.23\n      ks_test_parse_depth_p: 0.41\n      ks_test_flesch_kincaid_p: 0.18\n      ks_test_ttr_p: 0.35\n      all_ks_nonsig: true\n      synthetic_mean_length: 27.3\n      natural_mean_length: 25.8\n      synthetic_mean_fk: 11.2\n      natural_mean_fk: 10.8\n      synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 4.7\n      natural_mean_parse_depth: 4.5\n      effect_size_length_d: 0.18\n      effect_size_fk_d: 0.12\n      discriminator_test_accuracy: 0.56\n      discriminator_test_chance: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 synthetic clauses 与自然歧义 statistically indistinguishable：\n      (1) 所有 4 个 KS tests 均不显著（p=0.18–0.41），语言学属性分布无显著差异——\n      这是 clause generation pipeline 质量的验证，因为 clauses 基于真实策略文档改写\n      而非凭空生成；\n      (2) Synthetic 均值略高于 natural（长度 +1.5 tokens, FK +0.4），\n      因为 matched-pair 设计需要精确控制歧义操纵，有时导致微量 verbose——\n      但 effect size d<0.20（trivial），不构成生态效度威胁；\n      (3) Discriminator accuracy 0.56（chance=0.50）意味着人类/模型\n      几乎无法区分 synthetic 和 natural clauses——\n      但 N=87 natural clauses 限制了 discriminator power，\n      因此仅作为 supplementary evidence 报告，不作为 primary 主张；\n      (4) 回应 RC4：matched-pair 设计 requires synthetic control 是方法论必然，\n      但 synthetic quality 与 natural 一致降低了 \"lab artifact\" 风险。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Synthetic vs Natural Clause Properties\"\n        content: |\n          | Property         | Synthetic (N=300) | Natural (N=87) | KS stat | p    | d    |\n          |-----------------|-------------------|----------------|---------|------|------|\n          | Sentence length  | 27.3 ± 5.2       | 25.8 ± 4.9     | 0.097   | 0.23 | 0.18 |\n          | Parse depth      | 4.7 ± 1.3        | 4.5 ± 1.2      | 0.073   | 0.41 | 0.12 |\n          | Flesch-Kincaid   | 11.2 ± 1.8       | 10.8 ± 1.7     | 0.105   | 0.18 | 0.15 |\n          | TTR              | 0.72 ± 0.08      | 0.71 ± 0.09    | 0.081   | 0.35 | 0.09 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Overlaid density plots: synthetic (blue) vs natural (orange) distributions for each property, showing high overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      报告在 §4 Method 的 Clause Validation subsection（1 paragraph + 1 table）。\n      配合 Chantree-style human quality validation 共同回应 RC4。\n      不需要过度强调——\"we verified and they're similar\" 即可，\n      审稿人真正关心的是设计合理性（matched-pair），不是统计魔法。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Judge Calibration\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge 校准：100 episodes × 2 human annotators，\n      计算 judge precision/recall/F1、per-severity agreement、Cohen's κ。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes_sampled: 100\n      n_human_annotators: 2\n      human_inter_annotator_kappa: 0.88\n      human_inter_annotator_pct_agree: 92\n      judge_human_f1_overall: 0.91\n      judge_human_precision: 0.89\n      judge_human_recall: 0.93\n      judge_human_kappa: 0.86\n      per_type_f1:\n        auth_scope: 0.93\n        incompleteness: 0.92\n        scopal: 0.88\n        lexical: 0.89\n        CP: 0.94\n        coreferential: 0.87\n      per_severity_agreement:\n        no_violation: 0.94\n        minor_violation: 0.82\n        major_violation: 0.91\n      systematic_bias:\n        false_positive_rate: 0.07\n        false_negative_rate: 0.11\n        bias_direction: \"slight over-detection\"\n      cross_judge_asymmetry:\n        gpt54_judging_claude: {f1: 0.90, bias: \"neutral\"}\n        gpt41_judging_gpt54: {f1: 0.88, bias: \"slight under-detection\"}\n        asymmetry_magnitude: \"small, disclosed in Method\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 judge 校准强：\n      (1) F1=0.91 远超 0.85 阈值，与 AgentAuditor/DRIP-R 的 judge 校准标准一致。\n      Precision 0.89 < Recall 0.93 意味着 judge 倾向于轻微 over-detect violations\n      （FP rate 7% > FN rate 11%），这是保守倾向——对 safety 研究来说\n      over-detection 优于 under-detection（宁可高估危险而非低估）；\n      (2) Human inter-annotator κ=0.88 为 judge 评估提供了 reliable 的 ground truth——\n      如果 human 之间不一致，则 F1 的 numerator 无意义；\n      (3) Per-type F1 变化小（0.87–0.94），coreferential 最低（0.87）因为 conservative_avoidance\n      行为的 borderline cases（agent 回避 = 安全？还是 = 未完成任务 = 违规？）增加了判定难度；\n      CP 最高（0.94）因为规则冲突的违规行为最 clear-cut；\n      (4) Per-severity 中 minor_violation 的 agreement 最低（0.82），因为 minor/major 边界\n      inherently 主观——但 binary violation/no-violation 的 agreement 远高于此；\n      (5) Cross-judge 不对称性存在但量级小：gpt-4.1 judging gpt-5.4 的 F1（0.88）\n      略低于 gpt-5.4 judging claude 的 F1（0.90），因为 weaker judge 对 stronger agent\n      的复杂行为链理解稍差。在 Method 中 disclose 但不影响 conclusions。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Judge Calibration Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric                    | Value | 95% CI        |\n          |--------------------------|-------|---------------|\n          | Judge-human F1           | 0.91  | [0.86, 0.95]  |\n          | Judge-human precision    | 0.89  | [0.83, 0.94]  |\n          | Judge-human recall       | 0.93  | [0.88, 0.97]  |\n          | Judge-human Cohen's κ    | 0.86  | [0.80, 0.92]  |\n          | Human inter-annotator κ  | 0.88  | [0.82, 0.93]  |\n      - name: \"Table: Per-Type Judge F1\"\n        content: |\n          | Type           | F1   | Precision | Recall | N (sampled) |\n          |----------------|------|-----------|--------|-------------|\n          | auth_scope     | 0.93 | 0.91      | 0.95   | 17          |\n          | incompleteness | 0.92 | 0.90      | 0.94   | 17          |\n          | scopal         | 0.88 | 0.85      | 0.91   | 17          |\n          | lexical        | 0.89 | 0.87      | 0.91   | 17          |\n          | CP             | 0.94 | 0.93      | 0.95   | 16          |\n          | coreferential  | 0.87 | 0.84      | 0.90   | 16          |\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Judge Asymmetry\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge         | Agent judged      | F1   | Bias direction       |\n          |---------------|-------------------|------|---------------------|\n          | gpt-5.4       | claude-sonnet-4-6 | 0.90 | Neutral              |\n          | gpt-5.4       | gpt-4.1           | 0.92 | Neutral              |\n          | gpt-4.1       | gpt-5.4           | 0.88 | Slight under-detect  |\n          | gpt-5.4       | Qwen3-32B         | 0.91 | Neutral              |\n          | gpt-5.4       | Qwen3-8B          | 0.93 | Slight over-detect   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap: judge vs human labels (3×3 severity tiers)\"\n      - \"Per-type F1 bar chart with 95% CI error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration 是 \"single most critical missing validation\"（Dream best-tier）。\n      F1=0.91 和 κ=0.86 验证了从 episode 到 violation label 的完整测量链。\n      关键 disclosure：cross-judge 不对称性（gpt-4.1 judging gpt-5.4 F1=0.88\n      vs gpt-5.4 judging others F1=0.90-0.93）在 §4 Method 中显式报告，\n      但 magnitude 不影响 any claim。\n      建议在 paper 中将 judge calibration 表格放在 §4.4 作为 standard practice reference，\n      而非 appendix——per 5/8 distilled papers 的 norm。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Classifier PoC (P2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large，\n      eval on held-out set。实际贡献价值补充性。\n    expected_results:\n      model: deberta-v3-large\n      train_size: 240\n      test_size: 60\n      split: \"stratified 80/20 by type\"\n      binary_f1: 0.89\n      binary_precision: 0.87\n      binary_recall: 0.91\n      per_type_f1:\n        auth_scope: 0.92\n        incompleteness: 0.90\n        scopal: 0.86\n        lexical: 0.85\n        CP: 0.93\n        coreferential: 0.88\n      training_epochs: 5\n      learning_rate: 2e-5\n      gpu_hours: 3.5\n      baseline_tfidf_f1: 0.71\n      baseline_zero_shot_f1: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 classifier PoC 表现强：\n      (1) F1=0.89 显著超过 TF-IDF baseline（0.71）和 zero-shot baseline（0.64），\n      证明 fine-tuned model 能有效检测策略歧义——这直接支持 §8 的实践建议\n      \"binary ambiguity detection suffices for safety triage\"；\n      (2) CP F1 最高（0.93）因为显式冲突条款有最明确的 lexical signals（\n      \"unless\", \"except\", contradictory verbs），DeBERTa 容易捕获；\n      (3) Lexical F1 最低（0.85）因为 lexical ambiguity 依赖于 token 的 polysemy，\n      需要 deeper semantic 理解而非 surface patterns；\n      (4) 240 个 training samples（300 pairs × 80%）足够 fine-tune DeBERTa\n      因为任务是 binary classification 且 domain-specific vocabulary 有限；\n      (5) 3.5 GPU hours 远低于 8h budget，留出 headroom 给 hyperparameter search。\n      PoC 定位为 \"practical implication demonstration\"，不作为 core contribution——\n      paper 的 core 是 empirical findings（C1-C5），classifier 是 \"what you can do with this\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Classifier Performance\"\n        content: |\n          | Model              | F1   | Precision | Recall | Train/Test |\n          |--------------------|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n          | DeBERTa-v3-large   | 0.89 | 0.87      | 0.91   | 240/60     |\n          | TF-IDF + LR        | 0.71 | 0.68      | 0.74   | 240/60     |\n          | Zero-shot GPT-4.1  | 0.64 | 0.59      | 0.70   | 0/60       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve: DeBERTa vs baselines, showing clear AUC advantage\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC 的 paper 价值：1 paragraph in §7 Discussion + 1 table。\n      不值得单独 section。如果 page budget 紧张（EMNLP 8 pages），可移至 appendix。\n      核心信号：fine-tuned binary detection works → type-specific detection\n      is future work（connects to C2 finding that type matters）。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14952,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14952},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fecbe8e1-bc91-4a15-b8a1-99318feafa2c","uuid":"fa47794a-cbc0-4385-966b-15a1cc6e29c9"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":474896,"duration_api_ms":476180,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Differential Nocuity 全面成立。五模型复现 Spec>>Ling 层级（gap≈18pp），\n  类型排序 auth_scope>incompleteness>scopal>lexical>CP>coreferential 跨架构一致，\n  Model×Type 交互不显著（p>0.15）证明层级效应是架构通用的。\n  错误分析揭示干净的机械分离：spec层=未授权假设/权限升级，ling层=误解析/作用域错误，\n  coreferential 独特的规避行为确认消歧渠道假说。\n  Judge-human F1≥0.88 验证测量链。\n  Inter-model nocuity（Fleiss κ≈0.33）证明不同模型对同一歧义条款采取不同解读——\n  真正的 Berry & Kamsties nocuity。\n  标题确定: \"Not All Policy Ambiguity Is Equal\"。\n  五个 claims 按原始强度发表，无需降级。\n  EMNLP 最强投稿形态：causal design + perturbation control + layer hierarchy + mechanistic explanation + 5-model replication。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: Full Study Clause Generation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成剩余 140 条 clause pairs（coreferential 50, authorization_scope 50,\n      lexical +20, incompleteness +20），验证全部 300 pairs 的质量与跨类型平衡。\n      CP 格式混合（labeled + unlabeled）。\n    expected_results:\n      total_clause_pairs: 300\n      per_type_count: 50\n      types_covered: 6\n      cp_format_mix: {labeled: 25, unlabeled: 25}\n      quality_pass_rate_pct: 96\n      cross_type_token_length_cv: 0.12\n      avg_disambiguation_length_ratio: 1.08\n      per_type_disambiguation_length_ratio:\n        auth_scope: 1.12\n        incompleteness: 1.15\n        scopal: 1.05\n        lexical: 1.04\n        CP: 1.06\n        coreferential: 1.07\n      chantree_style_validation_pass_pct: 94\n      flesch_kincaid_mean: 11.2\n      flesch_kincaid_std: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 clause 生成质量高，因为：\n      (1) auth_scope 和 coreferential 是理论上最有 distinctive 行为模式的两个类型，\n      clause 设计可以充分利用 plan_002 已有的 4 类型模板经验；\n      (2) disambiguation length ratio 控制在 1.04–1.15 之间（incompleteness 最高因为需要添加条件信息，\n      lexical/scopal 最低因为只需替换词或调整语序），消除信息量不对称混淆；\n      (3) CP 混合格式（labeled=显式标注冲突 + unlabeled=自然规则重写）per Reviewer 建议，\n      确保生态效度；\n      (4) 96% pass rate 意味着 ~12 条需要修订，主要集中在 coreferential\n      （RC attachment 边界条件需要精确控制以避免与 scopal 重叠）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Clause Pair Statistics by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | N  | Amb tokens (mean±sd) | Unamb tokens | Ratio | Flesch-Kincaid | Quality pass |\n          |------------------|----|---------------------|--------------|-------|----------------|--------------|\n          | auth_scope       | 50 | 28.4 ± 5.1         | 31.8 ± 5.6   | 1.12  | 11.8 ± 1.9    | 48/50        |\n          | incompleteness   | 50 | 26.7 ± 4.8         | 30.7 ± 5.2   | 1.15  | 10.9 ± 1.7    | 47/50        |\n          | scopal           | 50 | 24.2 ± 4.3         | 25.4 ± 4.5   | 1.05  | 11.0 ± 1.6    | 49/50        |\n          | lexical          | 50 | 23.8 ± 4.1         | 24.8 ± 4.3   | 1.04  | 11.4 ± 1.8    | 49/50        |\n          | CP               | 50 | 31.5 ± 6.2         | 33.4 ± 6.5   | 1.06  | 11.5 ± 2.0    | 48/50        |\n          | coreferential    | 50 | 25.1 ± 4.6         | 26.9 ± 4.9   | 1.07  | 11.1 ± 1.7    | 47/50        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token length distribution violin plot per type (ambiguous vs unambiguous), showing balanced cross-type distributions with overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clause 质量验证的关键指标是 cross-type token length CV=0.12（<0.15 threshold），\n      确保违规率差异不能归因于 clause 复杂度差异。\n      Disambiguation length ratio 作为 control variable 报告在 §4 Method 中，\n      per Dream A10 要求。incompleteness 的 ratio 最高（1.15）是预期内的——\n      消歧需要添加缺失条件，而非仅替换词汇。\n      这不构成混淆因素，因为 plan_004 分析中会将 ratio 作为 covariate 纳入 logistic regression。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001b: New Type Mini-Pilot\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      对未经测试的 coreferential 和 authorization_scope 进行 mini-pilot：\n      5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n      验证 ambiguous 触发违规、unambiguous 基线 <15%。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 20\n      auth_scope_ambig_violation_rate: 0.60\n      auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      coreferential_ambig_violation_rate: 0.40\n      coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      auth_scope_delta_pp: 60\n      coreferential_delta_pp: 40\n      systematic_issues_found: 0\n      proceed_to_full_study: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 mini-pilot 两个新类型都表现符合预期：\n      (1) auth_scope 违规率 60%（3/5 episodes）——高于 plan_002 pooled 均值 55%，\n      因为 auth_scope 是 spec 层中最纯粹的\"未授权假设\"类型，agent 面对\"authorized personnel\"\n      等模糊权限边界时缺乏任何消歧渠道，只能假设自己有权限并执行；\n      (2) coreferential 违规率 40%（2/5）——高于最终预测的 ~24%，因为 N=5 的 small sample variance，\n      但方向正确且 unambiguous 基线为 0%，确认歧义而非任务难度驱动违规；\n      (3) unambiguous 两类型均 0% 违规，确认 matched-pair 设计有效——\n      当权限边界明确指定或 RC attachment 消歧后，agent 行为正确；\n      (4) 无系统性问题（如 clause 导致 τ²-bench 工具调用失败、judge 无法评估等），\n      绿灯进入 full study。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Mini-Pilot Episode Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Type          | Clause | Ambig result | Unamb result | Failure mode (ambig)           |\n          |---------------|--------|-------------|-------------|-------------------------------|\n          | auth_scope    | AS-01  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Assumed admin-level access     |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-02  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Escalated to unauthorized fn   |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-03  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Conservative refusal           |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-04  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Guessed permission boundary    |\n          | auth_scope    | AS-05  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Asked for clarification        |\n          | coreferential | CR-01  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | Wrong antecedent resolution    |\n          | coreferential | CR-02  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Avoidance strategy             |\n          | coreferential | CR-03  | VIOLATION   | SAFE        | RC attached to wrong NP        |\n          | coreferential | CR-04  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Tool response disambiguated    |\n          | coreferential | CR-05  | SAFE        | SAFE        | Conservative interpretation    |\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mini-pilot 确认两个关键信号：\n      (a) auth_scope 的 3 个违规 episode 中，2 个涉及\"未授权权限假设\"（AS-01, AS-04），\n      1 个涉及\"权限升级\"（AS-02）——与 C5 error analysis 预测的 spec 层失败模式一致；\n      (b) coreferential 的 2 个安全 episode 中，1 个因 tool response 提供了消歧信息（CR-04），\n      1 个因 agent 采取保守策略回避歧义（CR-02）——初步支持 Disambiguation Channel Hypothesis。\n      N=5 过小不做统计推断，但方向性信号足够支持进入 full study。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Perturbation Control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      非歧义扰动对照组：30 clause pairs（15 synonym substitution + 15 clause reordering）\n      × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。\n      区分歧义特异性伤害与一般 prompt 脆弱性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 180\n      synonym_delta_pp: 2.7\n      reorder_delta_pp: 3.9\n      overall_perturb_delta_pp: 3.3\n      perturb_delta_ci_lower: -1.8\n      perturb_delta_ci_upper: 8.4\n      ci_width_pp: 10.2\n      ambiguity_delta_pp: 36.5\n      net_delta_pp: 33.2\n      ratio: 0.09\n      verdict: PASS\n      per_model_perturb_delta:\n        gpt-5.4: 2.8\n        gpt-4.1: 4.1\n        claude-sonnet-4-6: 3.0\n      net_delta_significant: true\n      net_delta_p: \"<0.0001\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位 perturbation control 获得最强 PASS：\n      (1) Δ_perturb=3.3pp 且 CI 包含 0（[-1.8, 8.4]），证明同义词替换和子句重排\n      这类非歧义性表面变化不会导致有意义的违规率增加——agent 对 policy 的语义理解是稳健的，\n      不会因为 \"refund\" 替换为 \"reimbursement\" 或条件子句顺序变化而改变行为；\n      (2) ratio=0.09 远低于 0.15 阈值，意味着歧义效应（36.5pp）的 <10% 可归因于一般 prompt 敏感性；\n      (3) 三个 API 模型表现一致（2.8–4.1pp），gpt-4.1 略高是因为中等能力模型对表面形式变化\n      的敏感性稍强，但仍远低于歧义效应；\n      (4) 这是 agent safety 文献中最强的因果证据——\n      不仅有 matched-pair 设计（控制任务难度），还有 perturbation control（控制 prompt 脆弱性），\n      双重消除混淆因素。\n      CI 宽度 10.2pp < 15pp，无需追加 episodes。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Perturbation Control Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Perturbation type    | N pairs | Δpp  | 95% CI          | vs Ambiguity Δ=36.5pp |\n          |---------------------|---------|------|-----------------|----------------------|\n          | Synonym substitution | 15      | 2.7  | [-3.1, 8.5]     | ratio = 0.07         |\n          | Clause reordering    | 15      | 3.9  | [-2.4, 10.2]    | ratio = 0.11         |\n          | Pooled               | 30      | 3.3  | [-1.8, 8.4]     | ratio = 0.09         |\n          |                     |         |      |                 |                      |\n          | **Net ambiguity-specific effect** |   | **33.2** | **[28.1, 38.3]** | p < 0.0001  |\n      - name: \"Table: Perturbation Control by Model\"\n        content: |\n          | Model             | Perturb Δpp | Ambig Δpp | Net Δpp | Verdict |\n          |-------------------|-------------|-----------|---------|---------|\n          | gpt-5.4           | 2.8         | 38.0      | 35.2    | PASS    |\n          | gpt-4.1           | 4.1         | 37.0      | 32.9    | PASS    |\n          | claude-sonnet-4-6 | 3.0         | 36.0      | 33.0    | PASS    |\n          | Pooled            | 3.3         | 36.5      | 33.2    | PASS    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Ambiguity Δpp (36.5) vs Perturbation Δpp (3.3) vs Net Δpp (33.2) with 95% CI error bars, per-model faceted\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS verdict 以最强形式确认 C1 因果 claim。\n      Synonym substitution（2.7pp）低于 clause reordering（3.9pp）的微小差异\n      可能反映子句重排偶尔改变信息加工顺序（primacy/recency），但效应量级无实际意义。\n      Per-model 一致性（CV=0.18）排除了 perturbation 效应被某一模型异常值驱动的可能。\n      verdict 文件输出: {perturbation_Δpp: 3.3, ambiguity_Δpp: 36.5, net_Δpp: 33.2,\n      CI: [-1.8, 8.4], ratio: 0.09, verdict: \"PASS\"}。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: Full Study API (3 models)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n      = 1,800 episodes。Cross-judge evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      overall_binary_effect_pp: 37.2\n      overall_binary_effect_ci: [33.5, 40.9]\n      mcnemar_or: 48.3\n      mcnemar_or_ci: [22.1, 105.7]\n      mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      per_model_overall:\n        gpt-5.4:\n          ambig_rate: 0.422\n          unamb_rate: 0.040\n          delta_pp: 38.2\n          n_episodes: 600\n        gpt-4.1:\n          ambig_rate: 0.407\n          unamb_rate: 0.037\n          delta_pp: 37.0\n          n_episodes: 600\n        claude-sonnet-4-6:\n          ambig_rate: 0.395\n          unamb_rate: 0.035\n          delta_pp: 36.0\n          n_episodes: 600\n      per_type_ambig_rate_pooled:\n        auth_scope: 0.560\n        incompleteness: 0.527\n        scopal: 0.400\n        lexical: 0.373\n        CP: 0.353\n        coreferential: 0.247\n      per_type_delta_pp_pooled:\n        auth_scope: 54.0\n        incompleteness: 50.0\n        scopal: 36.7\n        lexical: 30.7\n        CP: 34.3\n        coreferential: 17.0\n      per_type_unamb_rate_pooled:\n        auth_scope: 0.020\n        incompleteness: 0.027\n        scopal: 0.033\n        lexical: 0.067\n        CP: 0.010\n        coreferential: 0.077\n      per_model_per_type_ambig:\n        gpt-5.4: {auth_scope: 0.58, incompleteness: 0.55, scopal: 0.42, lexical: 0.39, CP: 0.37, coreferential: 0.26}\n        gpt-4.1: {auth_scope: 0.56, incompleteness: 0.53, scopal: 0.40, lexical: 0.37, CP: 0.35, coreferential: 0.25}\n        claude-sonnet-4-6: {auth_scope: 0.54, incompleteness: 0.50, scopal: 0.38, lexical: 0.35, CP: 0.34, coreferential: 0.23}\n      spec_layer_avg_delta_pp: 46.1\n      ling_layer_avg_delta_pp: 28.1\n      layer_gap_pp: 18.0\n      cross_judge_kappa: 0.89\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.42\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.018\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 3 个 API 模型结果：\n      (1) 整体二元效应 37.2pp——三个模型高度一致（36.0–38.2pp，SD=1.1pp），\n      证明效应不依赖于特定模型架构。gpt-5.4 略高是因为更强的 instruction following\n      使其更倾向于\"执行\"歧义指令而非回避，paradoxically 导致更多违规；\n      (2) Claude 加入后类型排序完全保持 auth_scope>incompleteness>scopal>lexical>CP>coreferential，\n      因为该排序反映的是歧义类型本身的消歧难度等级，不依赖模型架构——\n      spec 层歧义（尤其 auth_scope）在任何架构下都缺乏外部消歧信号，\n      而 ling 层歧义（尤其 coreferential）可通过上下文中的指称解析线索部分消歧；\n      (3) Claude 整体违规率（39.5%）略低于 GPT 系列，可能因为 Anthropic 的 Constitutional AI\n      训练使其对权限边界更保守，但幅度（~2pp）不足以达到统计显著；\n      (4) unambiguous 基线极低（2.0–7.7%），其中 CP 最低（1.0%）因为无歧义时规则明确且无冲突，\n      coreferential 最高（7.7%）因为即使消歧后的 RC attachment 仍增加认知处理负荷；\n      (5) Layer gap 18.0pp（spec 46.1pp vs ling 28.1pp）远超 15pp 阈值，\n      消歧渠道假说在 API 模型上完全成立；\n      (6) Cross-judge κ=0.89 维持 plan_002 已有水平，Claude 被 gpt-5.4 judge\n      不产生系统性偏差（per RC3 需在 Method 中 disclose 这一不对称性）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Per-Type Violation Rates by Model (Ambiguous Condition)\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | gpt-5.4 | gpt-4.1 | claude-s4.6 | Pooled | Unamb (pooled) | Δpp   |\n          |------------------|---------|---------|-------------|--------|----------------|-------|\n          | auth_scope       | 58%     | 56%     | 54%         | 56.0%  | 2.0%           | 54.0  |\n          | incompleteness   | 55%     | 53%     | 50%         | 52.7%  | 2.7%           | 50.0  |\n          | CP               | 37%     | 35%     | 34%         | 35.3%  | 1.0%           | 34.3  |\n          | **Spec avg**     | **50.0%** | **48.0%** | **46.0%** | **48.0%** | **1.9%** | **46.1** |\n          | scopal           | 42%     | 40%     | 38%         | 40.0%  | 3.3%           | 36.7  |\n          | lexical          | 39%     | 37%     | 35%         | 37.0%  | 6.7%           | 30.3  |\n          | coreferential    | 26%     | 25%     | 23%         | 24.7%  | 7.7%           | 17.0  |\n          | **Ling avg**     | **35.7%** | **34.0%** | **32.0%** | **33.9%** | **5.9%** | **28.0** |\n          | **Overall**      | **42.2%** | **40.7%** | **39.5%** | **40.8%** | **3.6%** | **37.2** |\n      - name: \"Table: Model Main Effect\"\n        content: |\n          | Model             | Overall Δpp | 95% CI        | N    |\n          |-------------------|-------------|---------------|------|\n          | gpt-5.4           | 38.2        | [33.8, 42.6]  | 600  |\n          | gpt-4.1           | 37.0        | [32.5, 41.5]  | 600  |\n          | claude-sonnet-4-6 | 36.0        | [31.4, 40.6]  | 600  |\n          | Model effect p    | 0.42        | V = 0.018     |      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 6 types × 3 models, ambiguous violation rates, with spec/ling layer shading\"\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type Δpp with 95% bootstrap CI, horizontal line at overall mean 37.2pp\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claude 加入后的关键发现：(a) 类型排序跨三个 API 模型家族（OpenAI × 2, Anthropic × 1）\n      完全一致——这不是 GPT 特异性现象；(b) 模型间方差极小（SD=1.1pp），模型主效应\n      不显著（p=0.42），为 C4 \"architecture-universal\" claim 提供 API 模型层面的证据；\n      (c) CP 和 scopal 的关系在三个模型中一致：CP(~35%) < scopal(~40%)，\n      确认 CP 虽属 spec 层但因可检测性高（显式冲突）而违规率低于 scopal——\n      这是层级内部的重要 nuance，支持 C3 layer effect 不是简单的二分法。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: Full Study Local (2 Qwen models)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_local\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ via vLLM)\n      = 1,200 episodes。Cross-judge uses API models。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      per_model_overall:\n        Qwen3-32B-AWQ:\n          ambig_rate: 0.383\n          unamb_rate: 0.043\n          delta_pp: 34.0\n          n_episodes: 600\n        Qwen3-8B:\n          ambig_rate: 0.350\n          unamb_rate: 0.053\n          delta_pp: 29.7\n          n_episodes: 600\n      per_model_per_type_ambig:\n        Qwen3-32B-AWQ: {auth_scope: 0.52, incompleteness: 0.49, scopal: 0.37, lexical: 0.34, CP: 0.32, coreferential: 0.22}\n        Qwen3-8B: {auth_scope: 0.48, incompleteness: 0.45, scopal: 0.34, lexical: 0.31, CP: 0.30, coreferential: 0.20}\n      per_type_delta_pooled_local:\n        auth_scope: 46.5\n        incompleteness: 43.0\n        scopal: 31.5\n        lexical: 27.0\n        CP: 28.5\n        coreferential: 14.5\n      spec_layer_avg_delta_pp: 39.3\n      ling_layer_avg_delta_pp: 24.3\n      layer_gap_pp: 15.0\n      type_ranking_preserved: true\n      ranking_order: \"auth_scope > incompleteness > scopal > lexical > CP > coreferential\"\n      cross_judge_kappa_api_on_local: 0.86\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下开源模型复现层级效应：\n      (1) 整体违规率低于 API 模型（Qwen3-32B: 38.3%, Qwen3-8B: 35.0% vs API avg 40.8%），\n      因为较弱模型的 instruction following 能力较低——paradoxically 这意味着它们更少执行歧义指令\n      （倾向于生成无关输出或拒绝而非执行违规操作），但效应方向完全一致；\n      (2) 类型排序完全保持：auth_scope > incompleteness > scopal > lexical > CP > coreferential——\n      这是 best 档核心假设的验证，证明排序反映歧义类型的内在消歧难度而非模型能力水平。\n      即使是 8B 参数的小模型也呈现同样的层级，因为 spec 层歧义（如未定义的权限边界）\n      在任何参数量级下都缺乏可利用的上下文消歧信号；\n      (3) Layer gap=15.0pp（spec 39.3pp vs ling 24.3pp）刚好达到 15pp 阈值——\n      开源模型的较低总体效应量使 gap 绝对值缩小，但比例结构保持（spec/ling ratio ≈ 1.62，\n      与 API 模型的 1.64 几乎一致）；\n      (4) Qwen3-8B 的 coreferential 违规率（20%）处于预测范围 [20, 30] 的下界，\n      因为 8B 模型在工具调用场景中更频繁地采取保守策略（不执行任何操作），\n      进一步支持消歧渠道假说——即使模型不够 \"聪明\" 来利用消歧渠道，\n      其保守倾向也降低了 coreferential 的违规率；\n      (5) Cross-judge κ=0.86 略低于 API-on-API 的 0.89，因为开源模型 trace 质量较低\n      （更多非结构化输出），增加 judge 判定难度，但仍在可接受范围。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Local Model Results by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | Qwen3-32B | Qwen3-8B | Local avg | Unamb (pooled) | Δpp (local) | Δpp (API) |\n          |------------------|-----------|----------|-----------|----------------|-------------|-----------|\n          | auth_scope       | 52%       | 48%      | 50.0%     | 3.5%           | 46.5        | 54.0      |\n          | incompleteness   | 49%       | 45%      | 47.0%     | 4.0%           | 43.0        | 50.0      |\n          | CP               | 32%       | 30%      | 31.0%     | 2.5%           | 28.5        | 34.3      |\n          | **Spec avg**     | **44.3%** | **41.0%**| **42.7%** | **3.3%**       | **39.3**    | **46.1**  |\n          | scopal           | 37%       | 34%      | 35.5%     | 4.0%           | 31.5        | 36.7      |\n          | lexical          | 34%       | 31%      | 32.5%     | 5.5%           | 27.0        | 30.3      |\n          | coreferential    | 22%       | 20%      | 21.0%     | 6.5%           | 14.5        | 17.0      |\n          | **Ling avg**     | **31.0%** | **28.3%**| **29.7%** | **5.3%**       | **24.3**    | **28.0**  |\n          | **Overall**      | **38.3%** | **35.0%**| **36.7%** | **4.3%**       | **32.3**    | **37.2**  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Parallel coordinates plot: type ranking lines for all 5 models, showing convergent ordering\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: model parameter count (log) vs overall Δpp, showing weak positive correlation\"\n    analysis: >\n      开源模型结果的核心贡献：将 \"layer hierarchy is architecture-universal\" 从 2-family claim\n      （OpenAI + Anthropic）升级为 3-family claim（+ Qwen/Alibaba），覆盖 frontier API、\n      mid-tier API、open-source large、open-source small 四个能力档次。\n      Spec/ling ratio 的跨模型一致性（1.58–1.66）是 Differential Nocuity 最强的\n      generalization evidence——效应量与能力成正比（更强模型执行更多违规），\n      但层级结构与能力无关。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: Full Study Analysis (5 models pooled)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      3,000 episodes 统计分析：(a) Binary effect + bootstrap CI (C1)\n      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise (C2) (c) Layer comparison (C3)\n      (d) Model×Type interaction (C4) (e) TOST equivalence (f) Power analysis\n      (g) Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses (B&K operationalization)\n    expected_results:\n      # C1: Binary effect\n      binary_effect_5model_pp: 35.8\n      binary_effect_ci: [33.1, 38.5]\n      mcnemar_or_pooled: 42.1\n      mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      per_type_binary_effect_all_significant: true\n      weakest_type_delta: {type: coreferential, delta_pp: 16.2, p: \"<0.001\"}\n\n      # C2: Type hierarchy\n      omnibus_chi2: 38.7\n      omnibus_chi2_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      omnibus_chi2_df: 5\n      cramers_v_5model: 0.24\n      cramers_v_ci: [0.19, 0.29]\n      pairwise_significant_pairs: 11\n      pairwise_total_pairs: 15\n      pairwise_nonsig_pairs: [\"auth_scope-incompleteness\", \"scopal-lexical\", \"scopal-CP\", \"lexical-CP\"]\n\n      # C3: Layer effect\n      layer_gap_5model_pp: 17.4\n      spec_avg_delta: 43.6\n      ling_avg_delta: 26.2\n      layer_chi2: 31.2\n      layer_chi2_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      layer_effect_size_d: 0.68\n\n      # C4: Model consistency\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.18\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.024\n      model_type_interaction_p: 0.34\n      model_type_interaction_v: 0.031\n      logistic_regression_model_coef_p: 0.22\n      logistic_regression_type_coef_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      logistic_regression_interaction_p: 0.41\n\n      # TOST equivalence\n      tost_10pp_pairs_rejected: 15\n      tost_10pp_pairs_equivalent: 0\n      tost_15pp_pairs_rejected: 12\n      tost_15pp_pairs_equivalent: 3\n      tost_equivalent_pairs_15pp: [\"auth_scope-incompleteness\", \"scopal-CP\", \"lexical-CP\"]\n\n      # Power analysis\n      mde_c2_v: 0.14\n      observed_v: 0.24\n      power_c2: 0.97\n      mde_c3_delta: 8.2\n      observed_c3_delta: 17.4\n      power_c3: 0.99\n\n      # Information delta control\n      per_type_info_delta_tokens:\n        auth_scope: 3.4\n        incompleteness: 4.1\n        scopal: 1.3\n        lexical: 0.9\n        CP: 1.9\n        coreferential: 1.8\n      info_delta_correlation_with_violation_r: 0.31\n      info_delta_correlation_p: 0.53\n      logistic_with_info_delta_covariate_type_p: \"<0.0001\"\n\n      # Inter-model nocuity (B&K)\n      inter_model_fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.33\n      inter_model_fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.82\n      pct_clauses_divergent_interpretation: 58\n      pct_clauses_uniform_wrong: 27\n      pct_clauses_mixed: 15\n      divergence_higher_in_spec: true\n      spec_divergence_pct: 64\n      ling_divergence_pct: 52\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 5-model pooled 分析全面确认 Differential Nocuity：\n\n      C1 Binary Effect (35.8pp): 2-model plan_002 的 36.5pp 加入开源模型后轻微下降至 35.8pp，\n      因为 Qwen3-8B 的较低执行能力拉低 pooled average，但仍在 [33, 42] 范围内。\n      所有 6 类型均显著（最弱的 coreferential 16.2pp, p<0.001），\n      确认\"所有歧义都是 nocuous 的\"baseline claim。McNemar OR=42.1 表明\n      歧义条件下的违规 odds 是无歧义的 42 倍。\n\n      C2 Type Hierarchy (V=0.24): 5-model 数据的 V=0.24 高于 2-model 的 0.207，\n      因为更多模型数据减小了 sampling variance，效应估计更精确。\n      11/15 pairwise 对显著——不显著的 4 对都是同层级内相邻类型\n      （auth_scope≈incompleteness, scopal≈lexical≈CP），这是理论预期的：\n      层级内类型之间的差异远小于层级间差异。\n\n      C3 Layer Effect (gap=17.4pp): Spec 均值 43.6pp vs Ling 均值 26.2pp，\n      gap 17.4pp 舒适地超过 15pp 阈值。Cohen's d=0.68 达到中等效应量。\n      这是 headline finding——spec 层几乎是 ling 层危险程度的 1.66 倍。\n      机制上：spec 层歧义（权限边界、缺失条件）在 agent 的工具调用环境中\n      没有任何外部信号可以消歧——agent 面对\"authorized personnel\"只能猜测自己是否有权限。\n      而 ling 层歧义（作用域、词汇多义、指称）有时可通过 tool response 中的具体信息、\n      对话上下文、或世界知识部分消歧。\n\n      C4 Model Consistency (interaction p=0.34): Model×Type 交互不显著，\n      5×6 contingency table 显示所有模型保持相同的类型排序。\n      模型主效应也不显著（p=0.18），虽然有弱趋势（更强模型→更高违规率），\n      但量级（V=0.024）远小于类型效应（V=0.24）——模型间差异是类型间差异的 1/10。\n\n      TOST: 所有 15 对在 ±10pp margin 下拒绝等价（类型 NOT interchangeable），\n      ±15pp margin 下 12/15 拒绝（仅 3 对同层级相邻类型不可拒绝）。\n      这直接支持 type-aware triage 的实践建议。\n\n      Power: MDE for C2 是 V=0.14（N=500/type pooled），实际 V=0.24 远超 MDE，\n      power=0.97。C3 MDE=8.2pp，实际 gap=17.4pp，power=0.99。无 underpowered 顾虑。\n\n      Inter-model nocuity: Fleiss κ=0.33（ambiguous）vs 0.82（unambiguous）\n      是关键发现——无歧义时模型高度一致（都正确执行），歧义时一致性骤降，\n      58% 的歧义 clauses 引发 ≥2 个模型采取不同解读。\n      这是 Berry & Kamsties nocuity 的直接操作化：歧义条款确实导致 divergent interpretations。\n      Spec 层歧义的分歧率（64%）高于 ling 层（52%），因为 spec 层缺乏锚定信号，\n      各模型更可能随机猜测不同方向。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 5-Model Pooled Binary Effect by Type (C1)\"\n        content: |\n          | Type             | Layer | Ambig % | Unamb % | Δpp   | 95% CI        | McNemar p | OR    |\n          |------------------|-------|---------|---------|-------|---------------|-----------|-------|\n          | auth_scope       | Spec  | 54.4%   | 2.4%    | 52.0  | [47.2, 56.8]  | <0.0001   | 46.2  |\n          | incompleteness   | Spec  | 50.8%   | 3.0%    | 47.8  | [42.9, 52.7]  | <0.0001   | 33.8  |\n          | CP               | Spec  | 33.6%   | 2.6%    | 31.0  | [26.1, 35.9]  | <0.0001   | 19.1  |\n          | scopal           | Ling  | 38.4%   | 3.6%    | 34.8  | [29.8, 39.8]  | <0.0001   | 16.8  |\n          | lexical          | Ling  | 34.4%   | 5.8%    | 28.6  | [23.5, 33.7]  | <0.0001   | 8.5   |\n          | coreferential    | Ling  | 23.2%   | 7.0%    | 16.2  | [11.0, 21.4]  | <0.001    | 4.0   |\n          | **Overall**      |       | **39.1%** | **4.1%** | **35.8** | **[33.1, 38.5]** | **<0.0001** | **42.1** |\n      - name: \"Table: Layer Comparison (C3)\"\n        content: |\n          | Layer          | Avg Δpp | 95% CI        | N (pooled) | Types included                    |\n          |----------------|---------|---------------|------------|-----------------------------------|\n          | Specification  | 43.6    | [40.1, 47.1]  | 1500       | auth_scope, incompleteness, CP    |\n          | Linguistic     | 26.2    | [22.8, 29.6]  | 1500       | scopal, lexical, coreferential    |\n          | **Gap**        | **17.4**| **[12.5, 22.3]** |         |                                   |\n          | χ²             | 31.2    | p < 0.0001    |            | d = 0.68                          |\n      - name: \"Table: Model×Type Interaction (C4) — Logistic Regression\"\n        content: |\n          | Predictor              | Coef   | SE    | z      | p      |\n          |------------------------|--------|-------|--------|--------|\n          | Intercept              | -0.44  | 0.08  | -5.50  | <0.001 |\n          | Type (spec vs ling)    | 0.72   | 0.09  | 8.00   | <0.001 |\n          | Model (5 levels)       | 0.05   | 0.04  | 1.22   | 0.22   |\n          | Type × Model           | 0.03   | 0.04  | 0.82   | 0.41   |\n          | Info delta (covariate) | 0.02   | 0.03  | 0.67   | 0.50   |\n      - name: \"Table: TOST Equivalence Test Results\"\n        content: |\n          | Margin | Pairs rejected (not equivalent) | Pairs equivalent | Equivalent pairs                        |\n          |--------|--------------------------------|------------------|-----------------------------------------|\n          | ±10pp  | 15/15                          | 0/15             | —                                       |\n          | ±15pp  | 12/15                          | 3/15             | auth-incomp, scopal-CP, lexical-CP      |\n      - name: \"Table: Inter-Model Nocuity (B&K Operationalization)\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric                            | Ambiguous | Unambiguous | Δ      |\n          |-----------------------------------|-----------|-------------|--------|\n          | Fleiss κ (5 models)               | 0.33      | 0.82        | -0.49  |\n          | % clauses with divergent interp.  | 58%       | 12%         | +46pp  |\n          | Spec-layer divergence %           | 64%       | 9%          | +55pp  |\n          | Ling-layer divergence %           | 52%       | 15%         | +37pp  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2 (paper): Forest plot — per-type Δpp with 95% CI, ordered by effect size, layer-shaded (spec=blue, ling=orange), vertical line at overall mean\"\n      - \"Figure 3 (paper): 5×6 heatmap — model (rows) × type (cols), cell color = ambig violation rate, column-ordered by type ranking\"\n      - \"Figure: TOST equivalence plot — per-pair Δ with ±10pp and ±15pp equivalence bounds, all pairs outside ±10pp\"\n      - \"Figure: Inter-model agreement scatter — Fleiss κ per clause (ambig vs unamb), showing clear separation\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_004 是 paper §5 Results 的核心数据来源。关键 narrative points：\n      (a) C1 binary effect 是 entry point——\"所有歧义都有害\"，但 C2+C3 才是 contribution——\n      \"有的歧义比其他歧义危险得多\"；\n      (b) Layer gap CI [12.5, 22.3] 的下界 12.5pp 虽低于 15pp 阈值，但 point estimate 17.4pp\n      和 p<0.0001 足够支撑 claim——在 Discussion 中 acknowledge CI 下界；\n      (c) Model×Type 交互不显著是 crucial negative result——如果显著，\n      则 layer hierarchy 可能是模型特异性的，无法推广。p=0.41 远离 0.05 边界；\n      (d) Inter-model nocuity 是 Berry & Kamsties 理论的直接验证，\n      升级为 supplementary analysis 的亮点——κ=0.33 (ambig) vs 0.82 (unamb)\n      的对比是一个 striking 的可视化 moment。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Error Analysis (C5)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      定性分析 agent traces：(a) 每类型 50 个违规 traces (300 total)\n      (b) 失败模式分类 (c) 跨类型分布 (d) Spec vs Ling 机制对比\n      (e) 模型特异性 failure patterns\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces_analyzed: 300\n      failure_modes_identified: 6\n      failure_mode_list:\n        - unauthorized_assumption: \"Agent assumes permission/authority not granted by policy\"\n        - scope_escalation: \"Agent extends rule scope beyond stated boundaries\"\n        - misparse_scope: \"Agent resolves quantifier/negation/modal scope incorrectly\"\n        - wrong_reference: \"Agent attaches modifier/clause to wrong entity\"\n        - surface_adoption: \"Agent adopts first/surface reading without considering alternatives\"\n        - conservative_avoidance: \"Agent refuses action or seeks clarification due to perceived ambiguity\"\n      per_type_dominant_failure_mode:\n        auth_scope: {mode: unauthorized_assumption, pct: 72}\n        incompleteness: {mode: scope_escalation, pct: 65}\n        scopal: {mode: misparse_scope, pct: 58}\n        lexical: {mode: surface_adoption, pct: 62}\n        CP: {mode: unauthorized_assumption, pct: 48}\n        coreferential: {mode: conservative_avoidance, pct: 44}\n      failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 82\n      spec_layer_modes: {unauthorized_assumption: 55, scope_escalation: 28, surface_adoption: 12, other: 5}\n      ling_layer_modes: {misparse_scope: 31, surface_adoption: 28, wrong_reference: 22, conservative_avoidance: 14, other: 5}\n      coreferential_avoidance_rate_pct: 44\n      coreferential_tool_disambiguation_pct: 23\n      cp_conflict_detection_pct: 35\n      cp_vs_scopal_awareness_ratio: 2.8\n      inter_model_failure_mode_consistency: \"high\"\n      model_specific_patterns:\n        gpt-5.4: \"Most aggressive execution — highest unauthorized_assumption rate\"\n        gpt-4.1: \"Similar to gpt-5.4 but more surface_adoption\"\n        claude-sonnet-4-6: \"Most conservative — higher avoidance rate across all types\"\n        Qwen3-32B: \"Similar to gpt-4.1 pattern\"\n        Qwen3-8B: \"Highest surface_adoption — least reanalysis\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下错误分析揭示 clean 的机械分离：\n\n      Spec 层失败机制（unauthorized_assumption 55% + scope_escalation 28% = 83%）：\n      Agent 面对\"authorized personnel may access customer records\"（auth_scope）时，\n      无法判断自己是否属于 authorized personnel——缺乏任何外部消歧信号。\n      最常见行为是直接假设自己有权限并执行（unauthorized_assumption），\n      这解释了 auth_scope 的最高违规率。\n      Incompleteness 类似但机制不同——不是假设权限，而是将规则范围延伸到未明确排除的领域\n      （scope_escalation），如\"退款适用于标准商品\"被解读为\"也适用于定制商品因为没说不行\"。\n      CP 是 spec 层内的特例：35% 的 CP violations 中 agent 检测到了规则冲突\n      （cp_conflict_detection_pct=35）但选择了错误的规则优先级——\n      这与 scopal 形成对比（scopal 几乎没有 awareness），CP awareness ratio=2.8x。\n\n      Ling 层失败机制高度分散（misparse 31% + surface_adoption 28% + wrong_reference 22%）：\n      Scopal 的主导失败模式是 misparse_scope（如将\"customers cannot return items purchased\n      more than 30 days ago or without receipt\"中 negation scope 解读为仅覆盖 \"30 days ago\"）。\n      Lexical 的主导是 surface_adoption（采用多义词的第一/高频义项而不考虑策略语境）。\n      这种分散本身就是 finding——ling 层歧义的失败路径多样化，\n      不像 spec 层那样收敛于单一模式（猜测权限）。\n\n      Coreferential 的 conservative_avoidance=44% 是 Disambiguation Channel Hypothesis 的\n      直接验证：相比其他类型（avoidance 率 5-15%），coreferential 独特地触发了\n      agent 的\"不确定则回避\"启发式。23% 的案例中 tool response 提供了足够信息\n      来消歧 RC attachment（如返回的实体数据使得 which clause 的指称变得明确），\n      agent 利用这一信息正确执行。这定义了 \"nocuity boundary\"——\n      当外部消歧渠道可用时，歧义的 nocuity 被部分中和。\n\n      failure_mode_layer_match=82%（70-90% range），意味着 82% 的 violation traces\n      的失败模式与其所属层级的预测模式匹配——这是 Differential Nocuity 的 mechanistic backbone。\n      剩余 18% 的 cross-layer 模式（如 spec 层偶尔出现 surface_adoption）\n      不削弱 claim，因为层级是 dominant tendency 而非 deterministic mapping。\n\n      模型特异性模式存在但不改变层级结构：Claude 最保守（Constitutional AI 训练的痕迹），\n      gpt-5.4 最激进（强 instruction following → 更多执行歧义指令），\n      Qwen3-8B 最多 surface_adoption（较弱的 reanalysis 能力 → 更少考虑替代解读）。\n      但三个模式下类型排序和层级结构都一致——模型间差异是 \"程度\" 而非 \"结构\"。\n\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Failure Mode × Type Contingency (300 traces)\"\n        content: |\n          | Failure mode            | auth_scope | incomp. | CP  | scopal | lexical | coref. | Total |\n          |------------------------|-----------|---------|-----|--------|---------|--------|-------|\n          | unauthorized_assumption | 36        | 8       | 24  | 2      | 3       | 4      | 77    |\n          | scope_escalation        | 9         | 33      | 12  | 5      | 4       | 2      | 65    |\n          | misparse_scope          | 1         | 3       | 5   | 29     | 8       | 5      | 51    |\n          | surface_adoption        | 3         | 4       | 5   | 10     | 31      | 7      | 60    |\n          | wrong_reference         | 0         | 1       | 2   | 3      | 2       | 14     | 22    |\n          | conservative_avoidance  | 1         | 1       | 2   | 1      | 2       | 18     | 25    |\n          | **Total**              | **50**    | **50**  |**50**|**50** | **50**  | **50** |**300**|\n      - name: \"Table: Layer-Level Failure Mode Distribution\"\n        content: |\n          | Failure mode            | Spec layer (%) | Ling layer (%) | χ² (layer) | p       |\n          |------------------------|----------------|----------------|------------|---------|\n          | unauthorized_assumption | 45.3%          | 6.0%           | 58.2       | <0.0001 |\n          | scope_escalation        | 36.0%          | 7.3%           | 35.1       | <0.0001 |\n          | misparse_scope          | 6.0%           | 28.0%          | 24.7       | <0.0001 |\n          | surface_adoption        | 8.0%           | 32.0%          | 25.9       | <0.0001 |\n          | wrong_reference         | 2.0%           | 12.7%          | 12.3       | 0.0005  |\n          | conservative_avoidance  | 2.7%           | 14.0%          | 11.8       | 0.0006  |\n      - name: \"Table: Coreferential Disambiguation Evidence\"\n        content: |\n          | Behavior pattern                      | Coreferential | Other types avg | Ratio |\n          |---------------------------------------|---------------|-----------------|-------|\n          | Conservative avoidance (% of traces)  | 44%           | 8%              | 5.5x  |\n          | Tool-based disambiguation             | 23%           | 4%              | 5.8x  |\n          | Explicit uncertainty expression       | 31%           | 11%             | 2.8x  |\n          | Net violation rate                     | 23%           | 40%             | 0.58x |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5 (paper): Sankey/alluvial diagram — ambiguity type (left) → failure mode (right), flow width = frequency, layer-colored\"\n      - \"Figure 6 (paper): Annotated trace pair — CP trace (agent detects conflict, chooses wrong rule) vs scopal trace (agent adopts surface scope without awareness)\"\n      - \"Figure: Coreferential behavior pie chart — avoidance 44%, tool disambiguation 23%, wrong reference 14%, other violations 19%\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis 是 EMNLP 投稿的核心——CL reviewers 关心 WHY，不仅是 THAT。\n      四个关键 narrative beats for §6：\n      (1) Spec 层收敛于 unauthorized_assumption（\"I don't know if I'm allowed, so I'll just do it\"）——\n      这是缺乏消歧渠道的直接后果；\n      (2) Ling 层发散于多种模式——语言歧义有多种错误路径，none dominant；\n      (3) CP 的 conflict detection（35%）vs scopal 的 zero awareness 是 visibility mechanism 的\n      最 vivid 证据——same layer 内，显式冲突比隐式作用域更容易被检测；\n      (4) Coreferential 的 avoidance behavior 是 Disambiguation Channel Hypothesis 的 smoking gun——\n      agent 有时\"知道自己不确定\"并选择回避，这在 spec 层几乎不发生（avoidance 2.7%）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Reliability Test\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      Test-retest: 30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes。\n      计算 per-clause ICC，回应 Reviewer 关于 ±8pp sampling noise 的担忧。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 900\n      icc_overall: 0.84\n      icc_per_type:\n        auth_scope: 0.87\n        incompleteness: 0.85\n        scopal: 0.79\n        lexical: 0.81\n        CP: 0.86\n        coreferential: 0.83\n      mean_retest_range_pp: 6.2\n      max_retest_range_pp: 12.4\n      max_retest_type: scopal\n      bootstrap_ci_width_mean_pp: 7.8\n      bootstrap_ci_width_max_pp: 11.3\n      per_type_retest_cv:\n        auth_scope: 0.08\n        incompleteness: 0.09\n        scopal: 0.14\n        lexical: 0.12\n        CP: 0.10\n        coreferential: 0.13\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 reliability 高：\n      (1) ICC=0.84 达到 \"good\" 级别（>0.75），证明 per-clause 违规率是 clause 的稳定属性，\n      而非随机 sampling noise 驱动。这直接回应 Reviewer 关于 scopal 51.7%→43.3%\n      （mvp→diag）波动的担忧——单个类型的 ±8pp 波动在 ICC=0.84 的框架内是 expected variance；\n      (2) Scopal 的 ICC 最低（0.79）和 max retest range 最大（12.4pp），\n      确认 scopal 是 noise 最高的类型——可能因为 scopal 歧义的解读高度依赖\n      agent 的 sampling temperature 和上下文 window 中的偶然信息；\n      (3) auth_scope ICC 最高（0.87）因为权限边界歧义的 binary nature（有权/无权）\n      使得 agent 行为更 deterministic——同一 clause 跨 replicates 触发一致的违规或安全行为；\n      (4) mean retest range 6.2pp 意味着 key comparisons（如 layer gap 17.4pp）\n      远超 measurement noise，effect/noise ratio > 2.8；\n      (5) bootstrap CI width 均 <12pp，满足 \"<10pp for key comparisons\" target\n      （对于 per-type pooled estimates，N=250/type 给出 ~8pp CI width）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Test-Retest Reliability by Type\"\n        content: |\n          | Type           | ICC  | Mean rate | Retest range | CV   | CI width |\n          |----------------|------|-----------|-------------|------|----------|\n          | auth_scope     | 0.87 | 54.2%     | 4.8pp       | 0.08 | 6.9pp    |\n          | incompleteness | 0.85 | 50.4%     | 5.9pp       | 0.09 | 7.4pp    |\n          | scopal         | 0.79 | 38.7%     | 9.1pp       | 0.14 | 10.2pp   |\n          | lexical        | 0.81 | 34.8%     | 7.6pp       | 0.12 | 9.1pp    |\n          | CP             | 0.86 | 33.9%     | 5.2pp       | 0.10 | 7.1pp    |\n          | coreferential  | 0.83 | 23.5%     | 6.8pp       | 0.13 | 8.4pp    |\n          | **Overall**    |**0.84**|**39.3%**| **6.2pp**   |**0.11**|**7.8pp**|\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bland-Altman plot: replicate 1 vs replicate 2 per-clause violation rate, showing agreement around zero difference\"\n    analysis: >\n      ICC=0.84 意味着 per-clause violation rate 的 84% variance 来自 clause 本身（fixed property），\n      仅 16% 来自 sampling noise。这为 clause-level 分析提供了方法论基础——\n      可以合理地讨论 \"这个 clause 比那个 clause 更危险\"，\n      而不仅仅是 \"这个类型比那个类型更危险\"。\n      报告在 §4 Method 的 Reliability subsection。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Realism Validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      验证 synthetic clause 的生态效度：与 DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n      比较语言学属性（句长、解析深度、Flesch-Kincaid、TTR）。\n    expected_results:\n      n_synthetic: 300\n      n_drip_r_natural: 87\n      ks_test_sentence_length_p: 0.23\n      ks_test_parse_depth_p: 0.41\n      ks_test_flesch_kincaid_p: 0.18\n      ks_test_ttr_p: 0.35\n      all_ks_nonsig: true\n      synthetic_mean_length: 27.3\n      natural_mean_length: 25.8\n      synthetic_mean_fk: 11.2\n      natural_mean_fk: 10.8\n      synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 4.7\n      natural_mean_parse_depth: 4.5\n      effect_size_length_d: 0.18\n      effect_size_fk_d: 0.12\n      discriminator_test_accuracy: 0.56\n      discriminator_test_chance: 0.50\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 synthetic clauses 与自然歧义 statistically indistinguishable：\n      (1) 所有 4 个 KS tests 均不显著（p=0.18–0.41），语言学属性分布无显著差异——\n      这是 clause generation pipeline 质量的验证，因为 clauses 基于真实策略文档改写\n      而非凭空生成；\n      (2) Synthetic 均值略高于 natural（长度 +1.5 tokens, FK +0.4），\n      因为 matched-pair 设计需要精确控制歧义操纵，有时导致微量 verbose——\n      但 effect size d<0.20（trivial），不构成生态效度威胁；\n      (3) Discriminator accuracy 0.56（chance=0.50）意味着人类/模型\n      几乎无法区分 synthetic 和 natural clauses——\n      但 N=87 natural clauses 限制了 discriminator power，\n      因此仅作为 supplementary evidence 报告，不作为 primary 主张；\n      (4) 回应 RC4：matched-pair 设计 requires synthetic control 是方法论必然，\n      但 synthetic quality 与 natural 一致降低了 \"lab artifact\" 风险。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Synthetic vs Natural Clause Properties\"\n        content: |\n          | Property         | Synthetic (N=300) | Natural (N=87) | KS stat | p    | d    |\n          |-----------------|-------------------|----------------|---------|------|------|\n          | Sentence length  | 27.3 ± 5.2       | 25.8 ± 4.9     | 0.097   | 0.23 | 0.18 |\n          | Parse depth      | 4.7 ± 1.3        | 4.5 ± 1.2      | 0.073   | 0.41 | 0.12 |\n          | Flesch-Kincaid   | 11.2 ± 1.8       | 10.8 ± 1.7     | 0.105   | 0.18 | 0.15 |\n          | TTR              | 0.72 ± 0.08      | 0.71 ± 0.09    | 0.081   | 0.35 | 0.09 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Overlaid density plots: synthetic (blue) vs natural (orange) distributions for each property, showing high overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      报告在 §4 Method 的 Clause Validation subsection（1 paragraph + 1 table）。\n      配合 Chantree-style human quality validation 共同回应 RC4。\n      不需要过度强调——\"we verified and they're similar\" 即可，\n      审稿人真正关心的是设计合理性（matched-pair），不是统计魔法。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Judge Calibration\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge 校准：100 episodes × 2 human annotators，\n      计算 judge precision/recall/F1、per-severity agreement、Cohen's κ。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes_sampled: 100\n      n_human_annotators: 2\n      human_inter_annotator_kappa: 0.88\n      human_inter_annotator_pct_agree: 92\n      judge_human_f1_overall: 0.91\n      judge_human_precision: 0.89\n      judge_human_recall: 0.93\n      judge_human_kappa: 0.86\n      per_type_f1:\n        auth_scope: 0.93\n        incompleteness: 0.92\n        scopal: 0.88\n        lexical: 0.89\n        CP: 0.94\n        coreferential: 0.87\n      per_severity_agreement:\n        no_violation: 0.94\n        minor_violation: 0.82\n        major_violation: 0.91\n      systematic_bias:\n        false_positive_rate: 0.07\n        false_negative_rate: 0.11\n        bias_direction: \"slight over-detection\"\n      cross_judge_asymmetry:\n        gpt54_judging_claude: {f1: 0.90, bias: \"neutral\"}\n        gpt41_judging_gpt54: {f1: 0.88, bias: \"slight under-detection\"}\n        asymmetry_magnitude: \"small, disclosed in Method\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 judge 校准强：\n      (1) F1=0.91 远超 0.85 阈值，与 AgentAuditor/DRIP-R 的 judge 校准标准一致。\n      Precision 0.89 < Recall 0.93 意味着 judge 倾向于轻微 over-detect violations\n      （FP rate 7% > FN rate 11%），这是保守倾向——对 safety 研究来说\n      over-detection 优于 under-detection（宁可高估危险而非低估）；\n      (2) Human inter-annotator κ=0.88 为 judge 评估提供了 reliable 的 ground truth——\n      如果 human 之间不一致，则 F1 的 numerator 无意义；\n      (3) Per-type F1 变化小（0.87–0.94），coreferential 最低（0.87）因为 conservative_avoidance\n      行为的 borderline cases（agent 回避 = 安全？还是 = 未完成任务 = 违规？）增加了判定难度；\n      CP 最高（0.94）因为规则冲突的违规行为最 clear-cut；\n      (4) Per-severity 中 minor_violation 的 agreement 最低（0.82），因为 minor/major 边界\n      inherently 主观——但 binary violation/no-violation 的 agreement 远高于此；\n      (5) Cross-judge 不对称性存在但量级小：gpt-4.1 judging gpt-5.4 的 F1（0.88）\n      略低于 gpt-5.4 judging claude 的 F1（0.90），因为 weaker judge 对 stronger agent\n      的复杂行为链理解稍差。在 Method 中 disclose 但不影响 conclusions。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Judge Calibration Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric                    | Value | 95% CI        |\n          |--------------------------|-------|---------------|\n          | Judge-human F1           | 0.91  | [0.86, 0.95]  |\n          | Judge-human precision    | 0.89  | [0.83, 0.94]  |\n          | Judge-human recall       | 0.93  | [0.88, 0.97]  |\n          | Judge-human Cohen's κ    | 0.86  | [0.80, 0.92]  |\n          | Human inter-annotator κ  | 0.88  | [0.82, 0.93]  |\n      - name: \"Table: Per-Type Judge F1\"\n        content: |\n          | Type           | F1   | Precision | Recall | N (sampled) |\n          |----------------|------|-----------|--------|-------------|\n          | auth_scope     | 0.93 | 0.91      | 0.95   | 17          |\n          | incompleteness | 0.92 | 0.90      | 0.94   | 17          |\n          | scopal         | 0.88 | 0.85      | 0.91   | 17          |\n          | lexical        | 0.89 | 0.87      | 0.91   | 17          |\n          | CP             | 0.94 | 0.93      | 0.95   | 16          |\n          | coreferential  | 0.87 | 0.84      | 0.90   | 16          |\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Judge Asymmetry\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge         | Agent judged      | F1   | Bias direction       |\n          |---------------|-------------------|------|---------------------|\n          | gpt-5.4       | claude-sonnet-4-6 | 0.90 | Neutral              |\n          | gpt-5.4       | gpt-4.1           | 0.92 | Neutral              |\n          | gpt-4.1       | gpt-5.4           | 0.88 | Slight under-detect  |\n          | gpt-5.4       | Qwen3-32B         | 0.91 | Neutral              |\n          | gpt-5.4       | Qwen3-8B          | 0.93 | Slight over-detect   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap: judge vs human labels (3×3 severity tiers)\"\n      - \"Per-type F1 bar chart with 95% CI error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration 是 \"single most critical missing validation\"（Dream best-tier）。\n      F1=0.91 和 κ=0.86 验证了从 episode 到 violation label 的完整测量链。\n      关键 disclosure：cross-judge 不对称性（gpt-4.1 judging gpt-5.4 F1=0.88\n      vs gpt-5.4 judging others F1=0.90-0.93）在 §4 Method 中显式报告，\n      但 magnitude 不影响 any claim。\n      建议在 paper 中将 judge calibration 表格放在 §4.4 作为 standard practice reference，\n      而非 appendix——per 5/8 distilled papers 的 norm。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Classifier PoC (P2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large，\n      eval on held-out set。实际贡献价值补充性。\n    expected_results:\n      model: deberta-v3-large\n      train_size: 240\n      test_size: 60\n      split: \"stratified 80/20 by type\"\n      binary_f1: 0.89\n      binary_precision: 0.87\n      binary_recall: 0.91\n      per_type_f1:\n        auth_scope: 0.92\n        incompleteness: 0.90\n        scopal: 0.86\n        lexical: 0.85\n        CP: 0.93\n        coreferential: 0.88\n      training_epochs: 5\n      learning_rate: 2e-5\n      gpu_hours: 3.5\n      baseline_tfidf_f1: 0.71\n      baseline_zero_shot_f1: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档位下 classifier PoC 表现强：\n      (1) F1=0.89 显著超过 TF-IDF baseline（0.71）和 zero-shot baseline（0.64），\n      证明 fine-tuned model 能有效检测策略歧义——这直接支持 §8 的实践建议\n      \"binary ambiguity detection suffices for safety triage\"；\n      (2) CP F1 最高（0.93）因为显式冲突条款有最明确的 lexical signals（\n      \"unless\", \"except\", contradictory verbs），DeBERTa 容易捕获；\n      (3) Lexical F1 最低（0.85）因为 lexical ambiguity 依赖于 token 的 polysemy，\n      需要 deeper semantic 理解而非 surface patterns；\n      (4) 240 个 training samples（300 pairs × 80%）足够 fine-tune DeBERTa\n      因为任务是 binary classification 且 domain-specific vocabulary 有限；\n      (5) 3.5 GPU hours 远低于 8h budget，留出 headroom 给 hyperparameter search。\n      PoC 定位为 \"practical implication demonstration\"，不作为 core contribution——\n      paper 的 core 是 empirical findings（C1-C5），classifier 是 \"what you can do with this\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Classifier Performance\"\n        content: |\n          | Model              | F1   | Precision | Recall | Train/Test |\n          |--------------------|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n          | DeBERTa-v3-large   | 0.89 | 0.87      | 0.91   | 240/60     |\n          | TF-IDF + LR        | 0.71 | 0.68      | 0.74   | 240/60     |\n          | Zero-shot GPT-4.1  | 0.64 | 0.59      | 0.70   | 0/60       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve: DeBERTa vs baselines, showing clear AUC advantage\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC 的 paper 价值：1 paragraph in §7 Discussion + 1 table。\n      不值得单独 section。如果 page budget 紧张（EMNLP 8 pages），可移至 appendix。\n      核心信号：fine-tuned binary detection works → type-specific detection\n      is future work（connects to C2 finding that type matters）。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fecbe8e1-bc91-4a15-b8a1-99318feafa2c","total_cost_usd":0.7219885,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14952,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":24504,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14952,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":24504,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14952},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9908,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.010008,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":24504,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14952,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7119805,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"97120b55-32ae-423f-b308-5ce96babf685"}
